    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1338": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator, Planning and Decision Support",
      "description": "Category: Administrative JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU Office of Planning and Decision Support invites applications for an Office Coordinator. The Office Coordinator supports the Office of Planning and Decision Support's mission of providing centralized leadership and support for institutional planning, institutional research, institutional effectiveness, accreditation, assessment, academic program review, strategic reporting, and data-informed decision-making across the university. This position is responsible for coordinating daily office operations, including administrative support, budgeting, purchasing, records management, scheduling, personnel processes, and customer service. The Office Coordinator manages office finances and expenditures, maintains confidential personnel and financial records, supervises student employees, and ensures compliance with university policies and procedures. The position also supports assessment, reporting, and institutional effectiveness activities, including testing administration, state reporting, and collaboration with campus and external stakeholders. Additional responsibilities include coordinating meetings and special events, maintaining the office website, overseeing office maintenance needs, and providing operational support for strategic initiatives and projects that advance the university's mission. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of related procedures and systems. Computer skills. Customer service skills. Interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituents in a diverse community. Ability to gather data, compile information, and prepare reports. Ability to use tact and discretion when dealing with a variety of issues. Required Qualifications High school diploma and four (4) years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Compensation & Benefits Job Family: Administrative Associate 3 Salary Range: Market Range 4 For information on benefits please visit: www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume 3-5 references upon request University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1360": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Pharmaceutical Sciences (690150)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Position Overview The Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences in the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the Assistant Professor rank, with a preferred start date of July 1, 2027. We seek individuals who are passionate about high-quality, evidence-based teaching, innovative research, and fostering a collaborative academic environment. The successful candidate will contribute to the professional pharmacy (PharmD) curriculum through teaching and mentoring, maintain an active program of scholarship, pursue extramural funding opportunities, and engage in service activities that support the department, college, university, and profession. The position provides an opportunity to join a vibrant academic community committed to excellence in pharmacy education, research, and service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to deliver high-quality, evidence-based instruction in professional pharmacy education. Demonstrated commitment to student success, mentoring, and collaborative learning environments. Ability to establish and maintain a productive program of scholarship and research. Effective oral and written communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners across disciplines. Commitment to service and engagement within the academic and professional community. Required Qualifications Earned PhD in Pharmaceutical Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, or a closely related field by the date of appointment. Demonstrated record of and/or strong potential for excellence in teaching and scholarly activity appropriate to rank. Ability to contribute effectively to the professional pharmacy curriculum Potential to develop and sustain a productive research program and pursue external funding. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in medicinal chemistry, bioanalytical chemistry, immunology, biochemistry, or a related area within pharmaceutical sciences. Ability to contribute to multiple areas of instruction, including interdisciplinary teaching across pharmaceutical sciences disciplines. Experience in pharmacy education. Record of scholarly publications and/or success in obtaining extramural funding commensurate with rank. Compensation & Benefits Salary is nationally competitive and consistent with AACP guidelines. Salary will be commensurate with rank, qualifications, and experience. A start-up package is available. For information on employee benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should apply through https://jobs.etsu.edu and upload: • Cover Letter • Curriculum Vitae • Statement of Teaching Philosophy • Statement of Research Interests • Contact Information for Three Professional References For additional information, please contact Dr. Brooks Pond, Search Committee Chair, at pond@etsu.edu. About Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy East Tennessee State University (ETSU) Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy offers elite pharmacy training in Johnson City, Tennessee. The college is ranked among the top 5 accredited pharmacy schools in the nation and No. 1 in Tennessee for the North American Pharmacist Licensure Examination (NAPLEX) and Multistate Pharmacy Jurisprudence Examination (MPJE). Gatton has exceptional faculty who use a curriculum designed to prepare students to become the pharmacist of tomorrow, an integral member of the health care team. The college is part of ETSU Health, Tennessee's largest public academic health sciences center that serves the heart of health care for our region. University Overview East Tennessee State University is a comprehensive regional university serving approximately 14,000 students. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU is recognized for its commitment to teaching, scholarship, research, service, and community engagement. The university provides a supportive academic environment and serves as a hub for education, healthcare, innovation, and economic development throughout the region. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1374": {
      "title": "Part-Time Temporary Research Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: United States The Department of Internal Medicine Research Division seeks a Part-Time Temporary Research Laboratory Technician. The Part-Time Temporary Research Laboratory Technician will support ongoing research activities in the Nanomedicine Laboratory at ETSU, focusing on nanoparticle engineering, lipid nanoparticle (LNP) formulations, targeted drug delivery, and molecular biology. The technician will assist with laboratory experiments, cell culture, molecular and biochemical assays, nanoparticle preparation and characterization, data collection, and routine laboratory maintenance. The position requires hands-on laboratory experience, strong organizational skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively with research team members. This is a temporary part-time position, with a maximum of 29 hours per week. This position offers flexible scheduling based on laboratory needs and experimental activities. The hourly rate is $15.50 per hour , and is contingent upon external funding. Key Responsibilities Include: Perform mammalian cell culture, including cell maintenance, passaging, counting, and cryopreservation. Conduct molecular biology experiments, including DNA/RNA extraction, PCR, qPCR, and gel electrophoresis. Perform biochemical assays, including ELISA, Western blotting, and protein quantification. Conduct fluorescence microscopy, immunofluorescence staining, and cellular imaging. Assist with flow cytometry, cell staining, and cellular uptake analysis. Perform cell viability, cytotoxicity, transfection, and gene expression assays. Assist with nanoparticle synthesis, LNP formulation, and physicochemical characterization. Prepare laboratory reagents, buffers, biological samples, and experimental materials. Collect, analyze, and document experimental data and maintain accurate laboratory records. Maintain laboratory equipment, manage supplies and inventory, and follow laboratory safety protocols. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Biology, Biochemistry, Biotechnology, Biomedical Sciences, or a related field Ability to independently perform laboratory experiments and accurately document results Previous hands-on experience in a molecular biology, cell biology, or biomedical research laboratory (preferred) Experience with mammalian cell culture, PCR/qPCR, fluorescence microscopy, ELISA, and other molecular and cellular techniques. (preferred) Experience with nanoparticle preparation, characterization, and drug delivery systems (preferred) Knowledge, Skills, Abilities: Molecular Biology: DNA/RNA extraction, PCR, qPCR, RT-PCR, gel electrophoresis, and gene expression analysis. Cell Culture: Mammalian cell culture, aseptic techniques, cell seeding, passaging, and cryopreservation. Microscopy: Fluorescence microscopy, immunofluorescence staining, and image analysis. Biochemical Assays: ELISA, Western blotting, protein extraction, and quantification. Flow Cytometry: Cell staining, sample preparation, and data analysis. Cell-Based Assays: Cell viability, cytotoxicity, transfection, and cellular uptake assays. Nanoparticle Techniques: Basic knowledge of nanoparticle synthesis, LNP formulation, DLS, and zeta potential measurements. Data Analysis: Microsoft Excel, GraphPad Prism, ImageJ, and experimental data interpretation. General Skills: Laboratory safety, experimental documentation, troubleshooting, organization, and teamwork. Compensation and Benefits: Hourly Rate- $15.50 per hour/no more than 29 hours per week No benefits Application Instructions: Non-exempt positions must be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. This position is contingent upon external funding. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter and Resume ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
