    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1384": {
      "title": "Talent Acquisition Partner",
      "description": "Category: Human Resources JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Talent Acquisition Partner is an on-site position that supports East Tennessee State University’s recruitment and hiring efforts for faculty, staff, student, and temporary positions across assigned colleges and administrative units. This position serves as a resource to hiring managers and search committees by providing guidance on recruitment practices, position requirements, interviewing and selection processes, and established university hiring procedures. The position helps lead the recruitment effort, including holding intake meetings, posting, and offering the position. The position will work with the departments on developing effective recruitment strategies and support outreach efforts to attract qualified and talented candidates. This position will ensure that the recruitment and employment activities are conducted consistently following employment law, university policies, procedures, and applicable employment requirements while providing responsive and collaborative HR support to departments throughout the hiring process. This postion will provide support to the Quillen College of Medicine and/or the College of Nursing. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Working knowledge of human resources principles, practices, and processes. Working knowledge of recruitment, talent acquisition, employment, onboarding, and candidate selection practices. Working knowledge of applicable federal and state employment laws and regulations related to recruitment, selection, equal employment opportunity, affirmative action, accessibility, and employment practices. Ability to interpret and communicate established HR policies, procedures, and guidelines. Ability to evaluate applications and candidate qualifications against established position requirements and selection criteria. Ability to identify and utilize appropriate recruitment strategies and resources to attract qualified candidates. Ability to provide guidance to hiring managers and search committees regarding established interviewing, candidate evaluation, and selection practices. Ability to provide professional, responsive, and timely service to employees, supervisors, applicants, candidates, and other university stakeholders. Effective verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to gather relevant information and assist with resolving routine HR and recruitment matters. Ability to recognize complex, sensitive, or high-risk matters and refer them to senior HR staff or the appropriate HR specialist. Ability to exercise sound judgment and discretion when handling employee and applicant information. Ability to collect, organize, and maintain recruitment data and information to support hiring activities, reporting, and process improvement. Ability to review information for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with established requirements. Ability to organize work, manage multiple priorities, and meet established deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and the ability to learn and effectively use human resources information systems and other workplace technologies. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business, or a related field and two years of related human resources, recruitment, or talent acquisition experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Relevant training or professional certifications may substitute for some education or experience requirements. Preferred Qualifications Social media management and recruitment advertising Graphic design skills for creating flyers, job postings, and promotional materials Experience with Canva or similar design tools Ability to create engaging content for Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, and other social media platforms Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Human Resources Professional 1 Market Range - 6 Salary Schedules While our salary ranges provide a compensation framework, initial offers typically do not fall at the top of the range. Salary offers are based on each candidate’s qualifications, experience, and overall alignment with the position, while ensuring internal equity across the organization. For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions and additional details Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Documents needed to apply: Resume, cover letter, and references available upon request Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1382": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Philosophy",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies at East Tennessee State invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, lecturer position in Philosophy, beginning August 15, 2027. We offer an undergraduate major in philosophy and minors in philosophy, religious studies, ethics, and humanities. Due to recent growth in demand for courses in the general education core, we are excited to be looking to welcome a new colleague to join our department. The position carries a 4-4 teaching load, primarily sections of a course called Practical Reasoning, which introduces students to the foundations of formal and informal reasoning. Participation in the shared service responsibilities of the department is expected. Further administrative responsibilities include coordinating with other instructors of critical thinking courses within the department, as well as other units on campus, including the Center for Teaching Excellence, Center for Academic Achievement, and General Education Advisory Council, both to support other instructors and elevate the quality of critical thinking instruction within the department. The initial contract is for three years. The position is renewable but is not a tenure-track position. Lecturers at ETSU are eligible for promotion, based on established university criteria. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to teach courses related to the foundations of formal and informal reasoning. Ability to collaborate with other instructor within the department, as well as other units on campus. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Philosophy at time of appointment. Evidence of good teaching ability in relevant areas is required. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Documents needed to apply: CV Cover Letter Evidence of teaching ability Application deadline: January 31, 2027 ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1266": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Lighting Design",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary East Tennessee State University Department of Theatre and Dance invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Lighting Design to begin fall 2027. The successful candidate will teach classes in Lighting Design and related areas. The candidate will also be in the rotation to teach departmental general education courses as needed. The successful candidate will design lighting as part of the Department’s 4 to 5 show mainstage season; supervise and mentor student designers; participate in academic advising; conduct ongoing internal and external research/creative activity; serve on Department, College, and/or University Committees; and perform other service to the Department as required, including Department supported recruitment activities throughout the academic year. The growing Department has 90+ majors, offers a BA in Theatre with concentrations in Design and Production, Musical Theatre, Physical Theatre, Acting, and General Theatre. The Department is accredited by National Association of Schools of Theatre (NAST). Productions are performed in the new (2021) 53 million-dollar state-of-the-art Martin Center for the Arts located on the ETSU Campus. The Martin Center facility holds support and teaching spaces (Theatre and Dance Costume Shop and Scene Shop) and three performance venues—the 1200-seat ETSU Foundation Grand Hall, the 200-seat Powell Recital Hall and the 200-seat black box theatre known as the Bert C. Bach Theatre. ETSU Department of Theatre and Dance’s primary performance venue is the Bert C. Bach Theatre. The Bert C. Bach Theatre is equipped with a tension wire grid; all LED fixtures; ETC ION XE control console; and the Lighting Designer’s office is close to the stage. The black box space dimensions are 57’x57’ with the tension grid at 20’. For teaching, a Yeager scale model Lighting Lab with an ETC ION XE control console is located in another classroom building on campus (Gilbreath Hall). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A strong lighting design portfolio and proficiency in Auto CAD and/or Vectorworks are required. Excellent organization, communication, and collaborative skills are essential. Proficiency with LED and Moving Lights and experience with Musical Theatre and/or Dance Lighting are highly desired. The successful candidate should be capable of hanging and focusing lights and able to supervise and demonstrate techniques for students in the grid. Required Qualifications MFA in Lighting Design or related field, conferred by date of hire. 2 or more years of undergraduate theatrical design teaching experience are required. Will accept Graduate Assistant teaching experiences as part of the 2 or more years. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Musical Theatre and/or Dance lighting is highly desirable. Proficiency with LED and Moving Lights is highly desirable. Secondary expertise in another area of design such as Projection Design (Video Design), Sound Design, or other related areas is welcomed. Physical Demands Must be comfortable working on ladders, personnel lifts, and at heights up to 21'. Must be able to navigate stairs and uneven walking surfaces. Must be able to bend and lift up to 50 lbs Compensation & Benefits Salary: $64,000 For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Portfolio Statement of Teaching Philosophy and Approach to the Work Three Reference Letters Optional Documents Certifications Media File ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1362": {
      "title": "Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary The Facilities Department here at ETSU is seeking to fill a vacant position. Responsibilities include performing a variety of skilled maintenance and repair tasks, including carpentry, painting, plumbing, and masonry, as well as other related duties as assigned. Candidates must be available to work various shifts and schedules, with overtime required as needed. Employees may also be required to report to work during emergency closures or inclement weather, including performing essential duties such as snow removal, to ensure the continued operation and safety of facilities. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of methods, materials, and procedures used in general repair and maintenance work Knowledge of the tools, machinery, and equipment used to perform a variety of maintenance tasks Knowledge of occupational hazards and applicable safety precautions Ability to properly use, clean, maintain, and perform minor repairs on tools, equipment, and machinery Ability to follow instructions, assess situations, and make sound decisions. Ability to exercise good judgment in the proper use and conservation of materials Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with coworkers and other personnel Ability to plan, organize, and prioritize work assignments efficiently Required Qualifications High School diploma Six months minimum experience in building and facility maintenance, including carpentry, painting, plumbing, masonry, and other general maintenance and repair tasks OR An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered Preferred qualifications Completion of vocational education 2 years experience in trade services Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services General Maintenance 2 Market Range - 4 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. References available upon request ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
