      "title": "Plumber",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Performs skilled plumbing work across university facilities, including the installation, inspection, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of plumbing systems and equipment. Maintains domestic water, sanitary sewer, storm drainage, natural gas, and related systems to support safe, reliable campus operations and compliance with applicable codes and regulations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of plumbing systems, fixtures, valves, pumps, and piping materials. Ability to diagnose and repair plumbing problems. Knowledge of applicable plumbing codes and safety regulations. Skill in using plumbing tools and equipment. Ability to communicate effectively and provide customer service. Ability to work independently and prioritize tasks. Knowledge of plumbing codes, practices, and safety procedures. Ability to read blueprints and technical drawings. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED and one year of experience in commercial, industrial, or institutional plumbing maintenance. Valid Driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications Journeyman Plumber license. Experience with institutional or university facilities. Experience with backflow prevention devices, pumps, boilers, and water treatment systems. Experience using computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS). Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services Trades Specialist 1 Market Range - 4 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. References available upon request ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
