    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1349": {
      "title": "HVAC PM Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The HVAC PM Maintenance Worker performs preventive maintenance, inspection, testing, troubleshooting, and minor repairs of campus HVAC and mechanical systems. This position supports the university's preventive maintenance program by maintaining equipment reliability, energy efficiency, and occupant comfort. Work includes air handling units, exhaust systems, filters, belts, motors, pumps, coils, controls, and associated mechanical equipment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of HVAC systems and preventive maintenance practices. Ability to inspect, test, and maintain mechanical equipment. Ability to use hand tools, power tools, ladders, and testing equipment safely. Basic understanding of HVAC controls and energy conservation practices. Ability to maintain accurate maintenance records. Ability to communicate effectively and work independently. Ability to follow safety procedures and university policies. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and at least one year of experience in building maintenance, HVAC maintenance, mechanical systems, or a related field. Valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications Technical training in HVAC or mechanical maintenance. Experience performing preventive maintenance in commercial or institutional facilities. Experience using computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS). Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services Trades Specialist 1 Market Range - 4 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. References available upon request ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
