    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1342": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse, University Student Health Center",
      "description": "Category: Medical Practice JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU College of Nursing, Office of Practice invites applications for a full-time Registered Nurse for the ETSU Student Health Center located on the ETSU Johnson City, TN campus. The Registered Nurse (RN) is accountable to the Clinical Director and/or Nurse Manager for the assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of patient care in accordance with established nursing protocols. The RN ensures the evidence-based application of nursing principles, prioritizes patient safety, and provides comprehensive patient education. This role involves utilizing clinical expertise to promote health, prevent disease, and support recovery. Additional responsibilities may be assigned as needed to support the overall mission of care. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of advanced nursing skills and techniques. Knowledge of current developments in health-related areas. Knowledge of university policies and procedures. Ability to work independently and make decisions regarding patient care. Ability to operate equipment including: computer, autoclave, centrifuge, microscope, cash register, blood pressure units, otoscope, ophthalmoscope, electric thermometers, etc. Ability to communicate effectively with university personnel at various levels, students, parents, representatives of the community, and the medical community. Ability to maintain the confidentiality of patient records. Ability to keep records and reports. Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in Nursing. One (1) year of clinical nursing experience. Licensure as a Registered Nurse in TN or compact/multistate by time of hire. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Nursing. Experience in ambulatory care. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by the employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job across various settings in the classroom, simulation, clinical, and/or community. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, climb, reach, and balance. The employee may occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, and/or move more than 100 pounds. The employee must be able to perceive and respond to sounds and alarms; communicate effectively with others; and have a sufficient vision regarding near, distance, color, peripheral, and depth perception as well as the ability to observe and monitor situations in full and dimmed light. The employee may stand, walk, and/or sit in various settings for up to 7.5 hours at a time in addition to the preparation and closure of a clinical shift. Rapid mobility may also be required on occasion. Physical expectations of an assigned clinical facility may vary and be subject to change. Stress levels may be high due to frequently dealing with numerous students, patients, family members, and other healthcare providers. This position demands concentration and the ability to work in emotionally-charged situations. Compensation & Benefits Job Family: Medical Nurse 1 Salary Range: $53,112.67 (MR 7 entry level) For information on benefits please visit: www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume Copy of active RN licensure from the State of Tennessee or compact/multistate An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. College of Nursing Overview The College of Nursing is part of the University’s Academic Health Sciences Center, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is the largest in the State of Tennessee, offering multiple tracks for students enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs. The nurse-led clinics under the College of Nursing feature four Federally Qualified Health Centers and two Student Health Clinics. The largest Community Health Center in Johnson City provides primary care, behavioral health care, pediatrics, and women's health with an on-site Dental Clinic, Radiology Department, Lab, and Charitable Pharmacy. Area unhoused individuals receive a continuum of services at the Downtown Day Center. Two school-based clinics in Hancock County provide care for students, staff, and the surrounding community. ETSU students and staff are served by the University Health Center on campus, while the nurse clinic at University School serves that population. The College of Nursing Community Health Centers have received federal funding for more than 30 years, accepting all patients regardless of their ability to pay. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1320": {
      "title": "Pediatric Critical Care Physician",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary: East Tennessee State University (ETSU), Department of Pediatrics, in collaboration with the Medical Education Assistance Corporation (MEAC), Niswonger Children’s Hospital, and Ballad Health, is seeking a Pediatric Critical Care Physician to join our expanding division. This position offers opportunities to contribute across clinical care, medical education, and scholarly research within a collaborative academic and healthcare environment. Candidates will play an integral role in providing high-quality pediatric critical care while supporting the educational mission of ETSU and the ongoing growth of the division. Position is contingent upon external funding. Other Considerations for this Position: Providing clinical care for the 10-bed PICU. Actively participating in the pediatric ground and air transports for the region as we move toward a comprehensive designated center and expanding the service for pediatric sedations outside the operating room. As this Tennessee facility is designated as a Level 1 Adult Trauma Center with Special Pediatric Expertise, the pediatric intensivist will be an active participant with the pediatric trauma team. Educational Opportunities Include: Opportunity to teach the first and second-year medical students in the basic science program. Work with the third-year students during the general pediatric clerkship/PICU subspecialty rotation. Instruct the 4 th year students taking the pediatric ICU Selective/Elective. Supervise the pediatric residents on the three required PICU rotations. Formal lectures will be given to the pediatric residents, community and emergency room physicians, and at local/regional conferences. The pediatric critical care physician will be expected to participate in ongoing quality initiatives/quality assessments and will be encouraged to participate in research and other academic pursuits. Required Qualifications: MD/DO Completion of pediatric critical care fellowship at time of hire Must be BC/BE in pediatric critical care at time of hire Benefits and Compensation: Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with experience. For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) *J1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Required documents to attach: Cover Letter, CV, and Copy of Transcripts. About The Community: Bustling with a population of more than 60,000, Johnson City lies just west of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Northeast Tennessee. The rugged beauty of the Appalachian Highlands surrounds the thriving city that encompasses all of Washington County and parts of Carter and Sullivan counties. It is known for its rich history (Daniel Boone, David Crockett, Al Capone and railroads), cultural heritage (bluegrass music, quilts and storytelling), outdoor adventure area (hiking, whitewater rafting, rock climbing) and beautiful lakes and mountain vistas. Yet, the eighth largest city in Tennessee also boasts diverse economic and educational opportunities and has become a regional hub for health care, including medical and pharmacy schools associated with East Tennessee State University. The city is also home to a beautiful and historic Veterans Administration campus and hospital. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students with highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, and recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1339": {
      "title": "Pediatric Cardiologist - Assistant/Associate/Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Overview East Tennessee State University Quillen College of Medicine Department of Pediatrics is seeking a pediatric cardiologist to join our expanding cardiology division who can contribute to our excellent academic community in the beautiful Appalachian Highlands. Position Summary The pediatric cardiologist works closely with Ballad Health, the region’s health system encompassing 21 hospitals, of which Niswonger Children’s Hospital is the flagship pediatric institution for a catchment area of over 1 million people. Our referral area includes Northeast TN, Southwest VA, and portions of KY and WV. Key Responsibilities Provide inpatient and outpatient services to pediatric and adult with congenital heart patients. Pediatric cardiology consultation services for Ballad Health facilities. Competency in interpretation of transthoracic echos, including fetal echos, EKGs, stress tests for outpatient and inpatient services required. Interpretation of CMRI, CTs is optional. Develop and manage patient plans and post-op along with the option of remotely participating in referring hospitals at their combined cardiothoracic conferences. Academic responsibilities include teaching of medical students, pediatric residents, and adult cardiology fellows as well as academic pursuits Highlights Established Pediatric Clinic with a thriving outpatient patient base and pediatric hospital medicine program. 24-bed Pediatric Inpatient Unit staffed by 8 Pediatric Hospital Medicine physicians 10-bed PICU Level III 44-bed NICU Required Qualifications MD/DO BC/BE in Pediatrics and Pediatric Cardiology at time of hire Completion of Pediatric Cardiology Fellowship at time of hire Benefits and Compensation: Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with prior experience. For information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) This position is contingent upon external funding *J-1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) Calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Required documents to attach: Cover Letter, CV, and Copy of Transcripts Area Information Johnson City, Tennessee offers an excellent quality of life including: No state income tax Affordable cost of living Excellent schools Friendly college community that is a great place to raise a family Outdoor adventure including water sports, biking, and hiking High level of community activities including symphony, theater, regional music, and storytelling Close to Asheville, Knoxville and Roanoke Regional airport with direct flights available ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
