    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1329": {
      "title": "Addiction Behavioral Health Specialist",
      "description": "Category: Social Service JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Addiction Medicine Behavioral Health Specialist works with the Care Team to recognize and address psychological symptoms and conditions using the bio-psychosocial approach. Assess and treat individuals with mental, emotional, and substance use problems, including the use of alcohol, tobacco, and other drugs. Activities may include individual, group, and family therapy, crisis intervention, case management, client advocacy, prevention, and education. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to demonstrate reliability and responsiveness to patients, families, and team patients. Ability to demonstrate mutual respect and build a trusting environment with patients, families, and team members. Ability to participate towards a common goal, reinforcing individual capabilities. Ability to build on strengths. Ability to assess external factors that impact health and behavior. Ability to show empathy. Establish and maintain good working relationships with various stakeholder groups. Makes meaningful improvements to services, programs, and processes and organizational effectiveness that creates new value for patients and employees. Practice shared accountability between patients, families, teams, and partners. Share and receive information, concerns, and feedback in a supportive manner. Works collaboratively across disciplines and administrative functions across the organization and in the community. Required Qualifications Master’s in behavioral health field including social work, counseling, or psychology and LPC, LCSW, PsyD, PhD trained in behavioral medicine and health psychology concepts. Trained in social, systems and familial aspects of psychological and medical conditions Trained in behavioral medicine and health psychology concepts. Trained in social systems and familial aspects of psychological and medical conditions. Trained in substance abuse identification and treatment. Preferred Qualifications Two years ' experience working in a clinical setting. Preferred experience in working with individuals with addictions in the setting of group sessions, and individual, and family counseling. Compensation & Benefits Salary: MR 9 Salary Schedules Job Family: Social Services Professional 3 Benefits : ( Employee Benefits ) *This position is contingent upon the availability of grant funding. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days . The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter, CV, Three (3) Professional References, and Transcripts. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1327": {
      "title": "PRN Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Floater, Nursing Office of Practice",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU College of Nursing, Office of Practice invites applications for a PRN Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Floater to support multiple nursing clinics. The Pediatric Nurse Practitioner (PNP) provides advanced primary care services to pediatric patients in accordance with the Tennessee Nurse Practice Act. This role is responsible for assessing, diagnosing, and managing both acute and chronic health conditions across the lifespan in infants, children, and adolescents. The PNP provides comprehensive age-appropriate preventive health services, including health screenings, developmental assessments, immunizations, anticipatory guidance, and health education. The Nurse Practitioner maintains accurate and timely documentation of all patient encounters and clinical services provided. The PNP provides supervision and guidance to assigned clinical and support staff, fostering a collaborative and efficient care environment. Participation in quality assurance and continuous improvement activities is an essential part of the role, ensuring adherence to best practices and regulatory standards. A strong commitment to health equity and the needs of vulnerable and underserved populations is central to this position, reflecting the clinic’s mission and values. Work Location and Travel: This is a floating position that provides coverage at multiple clinic locations as needed. Employees report directly to their assigned clinic each workday. Travel reimbursement is provided only for travel to Hancock County. Position Status: This is a temporary position with the potential to become permanent based on organizational needs, funding, and employee performance. Permanent employment is not guaranteed. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of pediatric growth and development, age-appropriate health assessment, preventative care, immunizations, and the diagnosis and management of common pediatric acute and chronic health conditions. Knowledge of age-appropriate communication strategies and the ability to effectively communicate with pediatric patients and their families/caregivers. Knowledge of recognized standards of care. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Ability to organize and set priorities. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) with preparation in advanced practice nursing (PMHNP, FNP, ANP, PNP or other specialty as required for position.) Current unencumbered license as Registered Nurse in Tennessee or compact state. National certification in appropriate area. Certificate of fitness to prescribe. Two (2) years of experience in advanced practice nursing. Applicants without PNP preparation, a minimum of five (5) years of professional experience providing primary care to pediatric patients is required. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by the employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job across various settings in the classroom, simulation, clinical, and/or community. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, climb, reach, and balance. The employee may occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, and/or move more than 100 pounds. The employee must be able to perceive and respond to sounds and alarms; communicate effectively with others; and have a sufficient vision regarding near, distance, color, peripheral, and depth perception as well as the ability to observe and monitor situations in full and dimmed light. The employee may stand, walk, and/or sit in various settings for up to 12 hours at a time in addition to the preparation and closure of a clinical shift. Rapid mobility may also be required on occasion. Physical expectations of an assigned clinical facility may vary and be subject to change. Stress levels may be high due to frequently dealing with numerous students, patients, family members, and other healthcare providers. This position demands concentration and the ability to work in emotionally-charged situations. Compensation & Benefits Hourly rate based upon education and experience. Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents required to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume Copy of current unencumbered RN licensure from TN or multi-state. Copy of National Board Certification. Copy of Certificate of fitness to prescribe. An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. College of Nursing Overview The College of Nursing is part of the University’s Academic Health Sciences Center, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is the largest in the State of Tennessee, offering multiple tracks for students enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs. The nurse-led clinics under the College of Nursing feature four Federally Qualified Health Centers and two Student Health Clinics. The largest Community Health Center in Johnson City provides primary care, behavioral health care, pediatrics, and women's health with an on-site Dental Clinic, Radiology Department, Lab, and Charitable Pharmacy. Area unhoused individuals receive a continuum of services at the Downtown Day Center. Two school-based clinics in Hancock County provide care for students, staff, and the surrounding community. ETSU students and staff are served by the University Health Center on campus, while the nurse clinic at University School serves that population. The College of Nursing Community Health Centers have received federal funding for more than 30 years, accepting all patients regardless of their ability to pay. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1328": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Popular Literature and Director of English Secondary Education",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Literature and Language at East Tennessee State University invites applicants for the position of Assistant Professor of Popular Literature and Director of English Secondary Education. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position. The teaching load is three courses each semester (fall and spring). The director will teach two courses per semester in the fields of Popular Literature (e.g., graphic novels, science fiction, fantasy, horror, etc.) and English Education and receive one course release per semester to supervise Residency 1 and 2 (student teaching) in fall and spring. The appointment is available to begin fall 2027. The Director of English Secondary Education performs the following responsibilities: (1) mentors English teacher candidates, (2) develops courses related to English Education, (3) fosters relationships with partner school districts and local English teachers, and (4) acts as a liaison between the Department of Literature and Language and the Clemmer College of Education and Human Development. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in English or closely related field at the time of appointment Knowledge of current trends in Popular Literature Secondary English Education teaching experience Preferred Qualifications Publications and/or teaching experience in Popular Literature, Secondary Education, and/or Teaching Methods Experience working with high-needs students and/or traditionally underserved student populations Evidence of collaboration with stakeholders, such as students, teachers, and districts/counties Evidence of leadership in professional development Experience with trauma-informed teaching methods University teaching experience Compensation & Benefits Salary: $62,000 plus benefits For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Position open until filled. A priority review is given to applications submitted by November 2, 2026. Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. For the application process, applicants must complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Three Professional References (Include: name, phone number, and email address) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts for all degrees earned ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1011": {
      "title": "Temporary Office Assistant - Center for Community Engagement[978361]",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States General Scope of Work This position will support the work of the Center for Community Engagement. The Center oversees and coordinates an array of ETSU strategic priorities and programming aligned with ETSU’s mission to “improve the quality of life for the people of the region and beyond.” Broadly speaking, the Center leads and manages the Go Beyond the Classroom Quality Enhancement Plan, ensures ETSU is meeting all the standards to maintain the Carnegie Classification for Community Engagement, leads all aspects of the ETSU Community-Engaged Learning designation for courses and co-curricular experiences, and promotes the benefits of university-community engagement. Qualifications · Familiarity with a university campus structure and organization · Evidence of excellent writing and communication skills · Exceptional attention to detail and organization · Technical skills in using a variety of software tools such as: Outlook tools - Microsoft Word, Excel, Powerpoint, Forms; graphic design tools such as Canva; web development platforms, and Qualtrics Responsibilities Marketing and Communications: · Support the Center’s Communication Plan · Promote workshops and events · Update and maintain the website Assessment and Evaluation: Assist with implementing, monitoring, and evaluating Community-Engaged Learning initiatives Event Planning: Provide support for planning, logistics, and management for the many campus-based programs each year as well as external-focusing events. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1064": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology is seeking applications for one full-time, 12-month, tenure-trackAssistant/Associate Professor in Audiology. Preferred teaching and clinical interest areas include adult diagnostics, vestibular sciences, electrophysiology, and cochlear implants. For both positions, responsibilities will be divided across areas of administration, teaching, scholarship/research, and service. Other specific duties may include: Teaching: Provide direct clinical supervision of students Serve as the Instructor of Record for several graduate-level courses Serve as the Instructor of Record for undergraduate-level courses, including Anatomy and Physiology and Introduction to Audiology. Scholarship/Research: Engage in scholarship activities, including presenting research at conferences and publishing articles in areas of expertise Collaborate with other clinical faculty and academic faculty to promote the research goals of the department Service: Coordinate Admissions and Orientation for new students Advise the ETSU Chapter for the Student Academy of Audiology (SAA) Delegate and monitor student graduate assistant (GA) positions within the department Engage in service activities at the departmental, university, professional, and community levels Compensation & Benefits Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Check out the ETSU Human Resources Benefits page for additional information at: www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . . Required Qualifications Au.D. and/or Ph.D. in Hearing Science, Audiology, or related discipline Hold ASHA certification in audiology (CCC-A) and meet ASHA requirements for clinical supervision of students Eligible for Tennessee licensure to practice audiology and dispense hearing aids Preferred Qualifications Five (5) years of full-time experience as a clinical audiologist Three (3) years of experience supervising Au.D. students Teaching experience within an Au.D. program Application Instructions Interested candidates should attach a letter of introduction, current curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references to their online application. Review of completed applications is ongoing, with applications accepted until the position is filled ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
