    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1265": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neonatologist - Assistant/Associate/Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States JOB SUMMARY The Department of Pediatrics at East Tennessee State University, Quillen College of Medicine, is seeking a full-time Neonatologist to join this division at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor, and the rank will be commensurate with academic experience. This is a non-tenure track position. The position is a joint hire with Medical Education Assistance Corporation (MEAC). Responsibilities of the Neonatologist include providing clinical care for a 39-bed level III NICU with in-house nurse practitioners, outpatient high-risk neonatal follow-up, the teaching of medical students and pediatric residents, quality improvement, and academic pursuits. We have over 800 NICU admissions per year at Niswonger Children’s Hospital, with air and ground transport systems available. An active perinatology division for maternal evaluation and management is also present through the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. The review of applicants will continue until this position is filled. We offer a competitive salary and benefits package. Our region is located at the base of the Appalachian Mountains and offers excellent schools, a low cost of living, and a wealth of outdoor activities. Applicants may contact Dr. Jack Owens, Professor and Chief of Pediatric Neonatology, by email at owensjd@etsu.edu or call at 423-439-6222. *J-1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS At time of hire: MD/DO Completion of Neonatology fellowship. Board Certified in Pediatrics. BC/BE in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS Salary : Commensurate with qualifications and experience For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) *Note: This position is contingent on external funding. APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copy of transcripts Please note: Exempt positions are posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days . The closing date is subject to change without notice Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution's focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1305": {
      "title": "Librarian (Quillen College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Medical Library at ETSU’s Quillen College of Medicine is seeking an early-to-mid-career full-time medical librarian to provide information services supporting students, researchers, and faculty. This position will work closely with the senior faculty librarian team to provide instruction, support, and conduct research, plan and execute events, and support outreach activities. The position will also be expected to provide college and university service by joining appropriate committees or working groups. This is a new position being created due to an increased demand for support for medical student research and a newly increased medical student class size (100). The ideal candidate will already have professional experience and knowledge suited for assisting with those needs; these abilities will be further developed with support from the senior librarian team. Specific skills with PubMed, citation management, critical appraisal of evidence, conduct of research, active instruction, event planning, social media management, and/or project management would be highly desirable and will be expected to be further developed. The successful candidate must be able to work cooperatively and collegially with a wide variety of professionals and students. They must be able to communicate professionally and productively, with patience and respect for others. About the Institution and Location: The Medical Library and the Quillen College of Medicine are located on the beautiful and historic Mountain Home VA campus in Johnson City, TN. Quillen College of Medicine educates medical students, residents, and biomedical sciences graduate students. The College was founded in 1974 with a mission to train primary care physicians and to increase the number of doctors in rural communities. Johnson City, with a population of around 72,000, sits in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains and serves as a hub for regional outdoor adventures. In 2025, East Tennessee State University joined the Great Colleges to Work For Honor Roll. The university provides a variety of engaging cultural and other activities, including Broadway shows, independent film screenings, musical performances, art exhibitions, a fitness center, outdoor equipment rentals, and an annual Festival of Ideas. Essential Functions Duties for this position may include: Developing active instruction sessions for synchronous teaching as well as asynchronous instructional materials in a variety of media for dissemination to students, faculty, and others. Supporting others’ instruction as needed. Conducting annual new resident orientations for several specialties. Conducting research and scholarly activities examining issues related to information-seeking, library activities and services, evidence-based healthcare, and other issues broadly related to health sciences librarianship, as well as disseminating findings via publications, professional conference presentations, and other methods. Supporting medical student research through activities such as PubMed training, citation management instruction, guidance on general aspects of research, and connecting students to other research supports. Working cooperatively with members of the IRB, research office, and other relevant teams to holistically support student research. Contributing service to the college and university as appropriate for a faculty member by serving on committees or working groups. Conducting expert searches of the biomedical literature to aid clinicians, faculty instructors, residents, and others. Carefully documents searches for the purpose of service statistics tracking, scoping or systematic reviews, contracted services, or other projects/needs. Aiding in planning and execution of other library events related to wellness, outreach, community-building, or other activities. Supporting library social media channels with content ideas and execution; responsible for posts under the direction of the library director. Providing customer service at the library’s central service desk as needed. Developing book exhibit ideas and associated programming. Contributing to library outreach activities such as consumer/community health efforts, including planning and attending events (which may be outside of typical work hours). Contributing to the development of new educational, research, student support, and outreach services and programs, and carrying out those planned services. Developing strong professional relationships with students, faculty, and staff to support their needs and inform library activities. Providing mentorship to less experienced library team members, including support staff, student workers, library interns, or others. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong communication skills with a commitment to respect, empathy, and professionalism. Fosters teamwork across multiple settings and goals; functions well in a team. Commitment to ongoing professional development. Demonstrable competency with PubMed, including advanced search techniques using MeSH. Able to develop and deliver education with active learning methods and identifiable goals to fulfill educational objectives; responsiveness to feedback. Demonstrated ability to contribute to the library’s scholarly output, including research idea development, survey and qualitative research methods, publications, presentations, and support of colleagues in the same. General knowledge of the conduct and ethics of research. Able to successfully complete and renew CITI Biomedical Research training, HIPAA training, and any other required professional development. Knowledge of and careful attention to ethical, privacy, and compliance issues such as patron confidentiality, research data storage, HIPAA, ethical conduct of research, and grants compliance. Able to provide high-level customer service at the library’s service/circulation desk. Willingness to be adaptable in responsibilities as needs for the library, college, and university change over time. High level of attention to detail and ability to balance many competing priorities successfully while ensuring deadlines are met. Proactive in seeking support when needed for prioritization, time management, and skills development. Able to occasionally travel for professional events and outreach, including some nights/weekends. Able to meet the requirements to be appointed as faculty at the Assistant Professor rank and pursue future faculty rank promotion. Required Qualifications ALA-accredited master’s degree in library and information science At least three years of experience in an academic medical or health sciences library Demonstrated experience in research and dissemination, instruction, and program support Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Based upon experience Benefits: For more information regarding benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter, CV, and Copy of Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employe r University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1311": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Addictionologist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States This position is contingent upon the availability of grant funding. Job Summary This position is for a full-time physician who will serve as a core member of the faculty team in the Department of Family Medicine Addiction Medicine Fellowship. In this role, the appropriate candidate will supervise and teach fellows in a 12-month Addiction Medicine Fellowship as a member of a professionally integrated team, treating patients with the diagnosis of behavioral addictions and substance use disorders, and participating in meaningful activities related to scholarly advancement of the specialty and administrative needs of the program. The successful candidate will deliver a collaborative model of medical care in conjunction with counseling and therapy interventions. Responsibilities include: Provide initial medical diagnosis Identify medical and health risks Formulate appropriate differential diagnosis based on history, physical examination, and diagnostic testing Perform psychosocial assessments and mental status exams to referred clients and, when indicated, prescribe appropriate medications Record and review medication management in accordance with state agencies and third-party payer standards Complete accurate and timely documentation of observations, interventions, plan of care, referrals, and follow-up Remain current in best practices, motivate staff to provide quality care, and complete documentation in a timely fashion Make appropriate referrals to other health professionals and community agencies Contribute to continuing education of medical students, resident physicians, and community providers by serving as a role model, mentor, and resource for better understanding and management of substance use disorders and behavioral addictions Participate in scholarly activity in the form of presentations locally, nationally, publications and/or text chapters Supervise and guide the education of various learners in the clinical and academic spaces of the Fellowship. This includes Addiction Medicine Fellows, Resident Physicians, medical students as well as undergraduate and master's level students from various departments and colleges. Required Qualifications At time of hire, candidate must be Board Certified by the American Board of Prevention Medicine (ABPM) in Addiction Medicine; OR Completion of an ACGME-accredited Addiction Medicine Fellowship and eligible to take the ABPM Board Exam to certify in Addiction Medicine; OR Current Board Certification as an Addiction Psychiatry specialist by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN). Medical Degree from accredited college/university. An active DEA registration in good standing is required at the time of hire and must be maintained throughout employment. Currently licensed, or able to obtain a license by hire date, by the Tennessee State Medical Licensure Board, and such license is not/will not be restricted. No reportable items to the National Practitioner Data Bank within the last ten (10) years. Compensation & Benefits Salary is determined by relevant experience For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days . The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter, CV, and Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1318": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Costume Design",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary East Tennessee State University Department of Theatre & Dance invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Costume Design to begin fall 2027. The successful candidate will teach classes in Costume Design and related areas. The candidate will also be in the rotation to teach departmental general education courses as needed. The successful candidate will design costumes as part of the Department’s 4 to 5 show mainstage season; supervise and mentor student designers; participate in academic advising; conduct ongoing internal and external research/creative activity; serve on Department, College, and/or University Committees; and perform other service to the Department as required, including Department supported recruitment activities throughout the academic year. The growing Department has 90+ majors, offers a BA in Theatre with concentrations in Design and Production, Musical Theatre, Physical Theatre, Acting, and General Theatre. The Department is accredited by National Association of Schools of Theatre (NAST). Productions are performed in the new (2021) 53 million-dollar state-of-the-art Martin Center for the Arts located on the ETSU Campus. The Martin Center facility holds support and teaching spaces (Theatre & Dance Costume Shop and Scene Shop) and three performance venues—the 1200-seat ETSU Foundation Grand Hall, the 200-seat Powell Recital Hall and the 200-seat black box theatre known as the Bert C. Bach Theatre. ETSU Department of Theatre & Dance’s primary performance venue is the Bert C. Bach Theatre. The Bert C. Bach Theatre is a 57’x57’ black box theatre with two comfortably sized dressing rooms and a green room. The costume shop is a state-of-the-art teaching and production space with domestic and industrial level machines, including an embroidery machine, and a laundry facility dedicated to the Bach Theatre. Additionally, the costume shop features a separate dye room with a 40-gallon dye vat and a second dedicated laundry facility for dyeing. Storage space is located in the same hall adjacent to the costume shop; all are located on the main level of the ETSU Martin Center. Additional storage facilities are located on the main campus. All storage areas are new or newly refurbished. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A strong costume design portfolio that demonstrates expertise in the field is required. Excellent organization, communication, and collaborative skills are essential. Proficiency with digital and hand rendering techniques and experience with Musical Theatre and/or Dance Costuming are highly desired. The successful candidate should be capable of pattern drafting and/or draping and be able to supervise and demonstrate techniques for students in the costume shop. Proficiency with a variety of domestic and industrial machines is expected. Required Qualifications MFA in Costume Design or related field. 2 or more years of undergraduate theatrical design teaching experience are required. Will accept Graduate Assistant teaching experiences as part of the 2 or more years. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Musical Theatre and/or Dance costuming is highly desirable. Proficiency with modern costume techniques and equipment is highly desirable. Secondary expertise in another area of design such as makeup design, hair and wigs, or other related areas is highly desirable. Physical Demands Must be comfortable working in a fast-paced production environment. Must be comfortable working on ladders and at heights up to 10'. Must be able to navigate stairs and uneven walking surfaces. Must be able to bend and lift up to 50 lbs. Compensation & Benefits Salary: $64,000 For more information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Portfolio Statement of Teaching Philosophy and Approach to the Work Optional documents: Certifications Media File ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1258": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Physiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States ob Summary The Department of Medical Education at the Quillen College of Medicine of East Tennessee State University invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor rank faculty position in the areas of Physiology and Pathophysiology education to teach in an active learning-based medical education program. Applicants may choose either a tenure-track or non-tenure track position. We seek candidates with broad training in Medical Physiology and Pathophysiology and demonstrate ability for excellent teaching. Responsibilities will include teaching Physiology/Pathophysiology to medical and graduate students and management of the Physiology thread across Quillen’s organ-based systems curriculum. Preference will be given to those candidates with expertise in interactive learning pedagogies, knowledge of medical school accreditation standards, and educational scholarship. The successful candidate will contribute to the education of medical students within the foundational science curriculum, engage in scholarly activity in medical education or related fields, and participate in service that supports departmental, college, and institutional goals. We seek collaborative, learner-centered educators who are enthusiastic about using active learning approaches (e.g., team-based and problem-based learning) to promote student engagement, responsibility for learning, and clinical readiness, consistent with Quillen College of Medicine standards. Faculty are supported and promoted with the develop and dissemination of educational scholarship and research programs. This is an excellent opportunity with a competitive salary, state-of-the-art teaching facilities, and the commitment of the existing faculty to provide strong career mentoring. Our very collegial environment also extends to clinical departments and other colleges at ETSU. The university is a regional state-supported institution serving ~15,000 students. Quillen College of Medicine consistently ranks among the top schools nationwide for rural medicine and primary care education. Johnson City is located at the base of the scenic Appalachian Mountains and provides a friendly, small-town atmosphere with a low cost of living, excellent public and private schools, clean mountain air, light traffic and southern hospitality. Responsibilities Include: Developing course and session objectives linked to USMLE content and QCOM institutional educational objectives where physiology and pathophysiology are relevant. Planning, developing, and providing active-learning student materials. Planning, developing, and providing active-learning pedagogical modalities within the pre-clinical curriculum. Writing and modifying quality NBME-style questions with faculty and staff support to be used in both the classroom and assessment settings, ensuring fair and accurate evaluation of student learning. Collaborating with faculty across basic and clinical sciences to ensure content integration. Acting as a team member to ensure courses run smoothly. Work as a valued team member in implementing course continuous quality improvement. Mentoring and supporting medical students in their professional and clinical development. Participating in departmental and institutional service, faculty development, and curriculum committees. Contributing to academic scholarship through either educational or basic/clinical sciences-based research and scholarship. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Successful candidates must present evidence of an established record of, or demonstrate a strong potential for, effective Medical Physiology/Pathophysiology teaching. A commitment to work productively with a team of medical educators from other basic and clinical science disciplines. Evidence for realized and/or potential of productive scholarly and creative activity. Ability to teach medical and graduate students from all backgrounds. Effective use of interpersonal and communication skills that incorporate tact and diplomacy. Strong ability to cultivate collaborative and mentoring relationships, solve problems, think creatively, and resolve conflicts. Strong work ethic, and approachable leadership style, and a consistent focus on the college’s immediate and strategic goals. Experience and record that reflects excellent organizational skills, effective verbal and written communication skills, attention to detail and follow-through. Fluency with standard office software and email communication required. Knowledge of student and patient privacy regulations (FERPA, HIPAA). Required Qualifications Applicants must have: PhD in Physiology or closely related field, MD, DO, PharmD, or equivalent degree. At least 2-years of successful physiology teaching experience in higher education. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the medical or professional school level and at the Assistant Professor rank. Experience in innovative educational practices such as active learning pedagogy. Knowledge of undergraduate medical school curricular/accreditation standards. Experience with educational and/or basic science scholarship. Service Expectations: The successful candidate will participate in forms of departmental, college, and university committees; student mentoring and advising; curriculum development initiatives; and professional service activities. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Commensurate with experience For information on benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for at least a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter , CV, and Copy of Transcripts University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/967": {
      "title": "PRN Patient Care Specialist, JCCHC",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU College of Nursing, Office of Practice invites applications for a PRN Patient Care Specialist for the Johnson City Community Health Center. The Patient Care Specialist supports clinical operations in a healthcare setting by assisting nurses with direct patient care. Key responsibilities include administering injections, performing EKGs, collecting specimens, assisting with procedures and examinations, and completing carious non-professional nursing and clerical tasks. This role requires a solid understanding of basic nursing principles and practices. This is a temporary position with the potential to become permanent based on organizational needs, funding, and employee performance. Permanent employment is not guaranteed. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficient in using electronic health record (EHR) systems to perform daily clinical and administrative tasks. Strong verbal and written communication skills for effective interaction with patients, providers, supervisors, and coworkers. Professional telephone communication skills, including coordination with pharmacies, healthcare providers, and community agencies. Ability to clearly and effectively communicate patient needs to clinical providers. Committed to maintaining patient confidentiality and handling sensitive information responsibly in compliance with HIPAA regulations. Thorough understanding of and adherence to university, college, department and clinic policies and procedures. Professional demeanor and ability to represent the facility positively at all times. Effective team player with a collaborative mindset. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain quality control standards. Ability to remain calm and perform effectively in emergency situations. Strong organizational and time management skills to complete assigned duties efficiently. Knowledge of accepted nursing and clinical medical assistant (CMA) standards and practices. Familiarity with medical terminology, basic pharmacology, and the foundational principles of nursing. Basic computer literacy to support clinical operations. Skilled in delivering patient care in alignment with facility standards, protocols, and procedures. The employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodations, in a satisfactory and effective manner. Required Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. RMA, CMA (AAMA certification) or LPN. Current CPR/BLS card required. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by the employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job across various settings in the classroom, simulation, clinical, and/or community. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, climb, reach, and balance. The employee may occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, and/or move more than 100 pounds. The employee must be able to perceive and respond to sounds and alarms; communicate effectively with others; and have a sufficient vision regarding near, distance, color, peripheral, and depth perception as well as the ability to observe and monitor situations in full and dimmed light. The employee may stand, walk, and/or sit in various settings for up to 7.5 hours at a time in addition to the preparation and closure of a clinical shift. Rapid mobility may also be required on occasion. Physical expectations of an assigned clinical facility may vary and be subject to change. Stress levels may be high due to frequently dealing with numerous students, patients, family members, and other healthcare providers. This position demands concentration and the ability to work in emotionally-charged situations. Compensation & Benefits Job Family: Temporary Non-Academic Support 2 Hourly Rate: $18.88 Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume Copy of RMA, CMA (AAMA certification) or LPN licensure/certification An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. College of Nursing Overview The College of Nursing is part of the University’s Academic Health Sciences Center, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is the largest in the State of Tennessee offering multiple tracks for students enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs. The Department of Undergraduate Programs is home to over 45 full-time faculty and 700 students across five (5) tracks including the Traditional BSN, Accelerated BSN (Johnson City, Kingsport, Sevierville), LPN-BSN, and RN-BSN/Dual Degree. The Department of Undergraduate Programs boasts a record of excellence with 60% of faculty holding specialty certifications and a strong record of collaboration and successful student outcomes. All programs in the College of Nursing are fully accredited by the CCNE. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
