    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1312": {
      "title": "Digital Marketing Specialist, University Marketing and Communications (120360)",
      "description": "Category: Communications and Marketing JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU Office of University Marketing and Communications invites applications for a full-time Digital Marketing Specialist. The Digital Marketing Specialist is responsible for developing, implementing, optimizing, and measuring digital marketing initiatives that advance East Tennessee State University's strategic priorities, including student recruitment, retention, institutional reputation, academic program promotion, and community engagement. Working within the Office of University Marketing and Communications (UMC), this position supports the university's digital advertising, marketing automation, audience targeting, campaign analytics, and performance measurement. This position will play a key role in leveraging Salesforce Marketing Cloud, helping to establish processes, workflows, audience segmentation strategies, and customer journey automation that support university-wide communication goals. The Digital Marketing Strategist will support projects for Student Life and Enrollment, the Graduate School, and other campus stakeholders. In addition, this position is responsible for managing digital campaigns; maintaining tracking and measurement infrastructure; providing actionable insights through analytics and reporting; and ensuring digital marketing efforts are strategically aligned, accurately measured, and continuously optimized to achieve institutional goals. **Please note this is a 24-month limited-term contract position. ** Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with marketing automation platforms and customer journey development, preferably Salesforce Marketing Cloud. Experience with audience segmentation, retargeting strategies, and digital advertising best practices. Knowledge of digital advertising platforms, including Google Ads, Meta Ads Manager, LinkedIn Campaign Manager, YouTube Ads, and other paid media channels. Ability to analyze campaign performance data and translate findings into actionable strategies that inform web and marketing decisions. Knowledge of Google Analytics (GA4), Google Data Studio, and Google Search Console, including the ability to build custom reports and dashboards. Basic understanding of Google Tag Manager, including creating and managing tags, triggers, and variables for event tracking and pixel implementation. Basic understanding of web code, including HTML, CSS, and PHP, sufficient to implement tracking scripts, troubleshoot tag-firing issues, and communicate effectively with developers. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple projects and priorities in a deadline-driven environment. Ability to collaborate effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders across the university. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Digital Media, Advertising, Communications, Information Systems, Business, or related field and three (3) years of professional experience in digital marketing, marketing automation, and organic and paid digital advertising campaigns across multiple platforms. Experience with salesforce Marketing Cloud, Marketing Cloud Account Engagement (Pardot), or compatible marketing automation platforms. Experience with CRM-based audience segmentation and lifecycle marketing strategies. Experience managing marketing projects and working with multiple stakeholders. OR A combination of education and work experience Preferred Qualifications Experience in a higher education environment Experience utilizing Google Analytics and campaign reporting tools. Experience with Google Tag Manager and conversion tracking implementation. Experience creating dashboards and reports using Data Studio or comparable business intelligence tools. Familiarity with CMS platforms such as Drupal, Webflow, Moderon Campus, or similar, particularly in an institutional or enterprise context. Google Ads, Google Analytics, Salesforce, of related digital marketing certifications. Compensation & Benefits Job Family: Communications and Marketing Professional 2 Salary Range: $53, 112.67 (MR 7) For information on benefits please visit: www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume 3-5 references upon request An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1275": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Director",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Psychology at East Tennessee State University invites applications for the Director of the ETSU Behavioral Health and Wellness Clinic (BHWC), the on-campus training clinic for the APA-accredited Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology. This position works collaboratively with the Director of Clinical Training and clinical faculty to support the BHWC’s dual mission of providing high-quality behavioral health services and professionally meaningful training experiences for doctoral students in clinical psychology. Primary responsibilities include developing, coordinating, and overseeing the activities of the BHWC; pursuing established clinic goals related to client services and graduate clinical training; supervising clinic office staff and contracted supervisory personnel, as needed; and coordinating clinical supervision for doctoral practicum students training within the clinic and, when appropriately credentialed, providing clinical supervision within the scope of the Clinic Director’s professional licensure. The Clinic Director also teaches graduate-level coursework related to clinical practice, advises the Director of Clinical Training regarding emerging training needs and professional practice issues, and in coordination with the DCT, may assist with relationships involving external clinical training and service facilities. Additional responsibilities may include oversight of clinic operational systems and processes that support the delivery of training and services within the BHWC. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Commitment to ethical practice consistent with the APA code of ethics. Ability to work effectively with populations in a positive, collaborative, and task-oriented manner. Ability to work collegially and collaboratively as a member of a clinical training program team. Knowledge of trends and developments in behavioral health practice and graduate clinical training. Ability to support graduate clinical training and coordinate clinical supervision within a multidisciplinary behavioral health training environment Provision of clinical supervision and instruction when appropriate to the individual’s professional credentials and scope of practice. Knowledge of the provisions of the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA). Interest in and willingness to develop expertise in rural and/or primary care settings, and integrated models of training. Knowledge of, and ability to learn, software and systems necessary to support clinic operations, including electronic health records (EHR)s, scheduling systems, BHWC website monitoring, and development/maintenance of BHWC promotional materials. Required Qualifications At least a Master’s degree in counseling, psychology, social work, or a closely related field. Applicants must be licensed or license-eligible as an LPC-MHSP, LCSW, LMFT, or HSP psychologist in the State of Tennessee. Preferred Qualifications At least two years’ experience practicing as a fully credentialed behavioral health professional. Previous clinic administration. Ph.D., Ed.D., or Psy.D. in (Clinical/Counseling) Psychology from an APA-accredited program. APA-accredited internship in clinical or counseling psychology. Benefits For information on benefits please visit https://www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Important Notes Faculty Designation & Rank will be determined based on qualifications. Cover letter should speak to how applicant’s personal credentialing can support the BHWC’s dual mission of providing high-quality behavioral health services and professionally meaningful training experiences for doctoral students in clinical psychology. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1283": {
      "title": "Temp Faculty COE",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary Temporary Position The Department of Psychiatry is seeking a board-certified child and adolescent psychiatrist with documented expertise in the child welfare population, needed to work with the Center of Excellence for Children in State Custody. This position will handle child and adolescent psychiatric consultations and evaluations with child welfare-involved children with complex needs. Required Qualifications Degree: MD or DO Certification: Board-certified or Board-eligible Licensure: Eligible for licensure in Tennessee Malpractice Requirements: Must meet ETSU Health malpractice insurance requirements ($5 million coverage) Salary - $6,651.12 a month. Application Instructions Non-exempt positions must be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter and CV. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
