    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1289": {
      "title": "Director of Residential Experience",
      "description": "Category: Student Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Director of Residential Experience is a full-time, 12-month professional staff member responsible for providing leadership, strategic direction, and long-term planning for a complex residential program serving approximately 3,365 students. Reporting to the Executive Director of Housing and Residence Life, the Director directly supervises two Associate Directors and provides indirect supervision and work direction to five full-time professional staff members and one security guard. As a member of the department’s senior leadership team, the Director collaborates with Housing Operations, Facilities, and Business Services to ensure that residence life programs align with departmental and university priorities. The position develops, assesses, and revises residence life policies and procedures; responds to concerns from students and families; and represents residential needs and initiatives in divisional leadership meetings. The Director builds partnerships across the Division of Student Life and Enrollment to support student success and serves as the department’s primary liaison to the Dean of Students Office regarding student conduct, crisis response, and critical student support. The position also coordinates with faculty, Academic Advisement, the Jordan Center, and other university partners. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of university housing operations, policies, procedures, and applicable regulatory requirements. Knowledge of student development theory and its application within a residential education environment. Knowledge of crisis intervention, emergency response, and behavioral threat-management practices. Knowledge of student conduct principles, policies, and procedures, with the ability to address conduct matters using a developmental and educational approach. Skill in providing strategic leadership and aligning residence life programs and services with departmental and university priorities. Skill in strategic planning, program assessment, and data-informed decision-making. Skill in leading, developing, and evaluating professional and student staff. Skill in fostering an inclusive residential environment and effectively supporting students from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Skill in developing, administering, and analyzing budgets and allocating resources effectively. Skill in managing complex projects and organizing, prioritizing, and completing multiple assignments within established deadlines. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, including the ability to facilitate sensitive or challenging conversations. Ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, university leadership, and external constituents. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and respond calmly and appropriately in sensitive, urgent, or crisis situations. Ability to build productive working relationships and contribute effectively within a collaborative leadership team. Ability to learn and integrate new technologies, hardware, and software to improve operational effectiveness and efficiency. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position, including: Observing and assessing residential environments and responding appropriately to routine and emergency situations. Communicating effectively with students, staff, supervisors, and emergency personnel during routine and crisis interactions. Using keys, access-control devices, elevators, telephones, computers, and other job-related systems and equipment. Accessing and responding to situations throughout residential facilities, including student rooms, bathrooms, hallways, stairwells, elevators, and building lobbies. Ability to support the university’s mission, vision, and values through the performance of assigned responsibilities. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education administration, student development, social work, counseling, or a related field and five (5) or more years of relevant progressively responsible experience at the professional, full-time level. OR Five years of work experience with a social services program. OR A combination of education and work experience. Successful completion of a background check required as a condition of employment. Preferred Qualifications Experience in residence life, residential education, housing operations, or student development within a higher education setting. Demonstrated ability to supervise professional staff and support their growth through coaching and feedback. Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Physical Demands (as needed) Sitting for extended periods (e.g., at a computer or workstation) Climbing stairs or ladders Reaching overhead or below waist level Carrying files, equipment, or supplies short distances Pushing or pulling carts, furniture, or equipment Frequent typing or keyboard use Visual acuity to read printed and electronic materials Hearing to distinguish sounds (e.g., phone calls, alarms) Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Student Services Management 2 Salary: Market Range 9 (Salary Schedules) For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1290": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Residence Life",
      "description": "Category: Student Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Associate Directors of Residential Experience are full-time, 12-month professional staff members, providing leadership and long-term planning for a residential area between 1,500 and 2,500 students, focused on either first-year students or returning residential students. The Associate Directors supervise between 2-3 full-time, 12-month, professional staff members, and oversees supervision of graduate and undergraduate staff members supervised at the Area Coordinator level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of housing and university policies and procedures. Knowledge of student development theories. Knowledge of crisis intervention procedures. Demonstrated ability to organize and prioritize multiple and detailed tasks. Skill in strategic planning and data-driven decision making. Skill in leading diverse teams and supporting diverse student communities. Ability to manage budgets and perform budget analysis. Demonstrated understanding of student conduct policies and procedures, including experience handling student conduct matters from a developmental perspective. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate and facilitate conversations with a variety of persons, including students, faculty, staff, parents, and outside constituents. Friendly, welcoming, positive, and a team player. Ability to effectively complete the various components of the Assistant Director position, including the following physical requirements: Visually access the community, surroundings, and situations that occur spontaneously and respond appropriately. Verbally communicate with staff, residents, and supervisors in casual and crisis interactions. Use and operate keys/access cards, elevators, phones, and computer systems. Access and respond to situations where they occur (i.e. inside student rooms, bathrooms, hallways, stairwells, elevators, and building lobbies). Ability to learn and effectively assimilate new technologies, hardware, and software into daily functions, especially to promote effectiveness and increase efficiency. Ability to contribute to the ETSU mission and vision and live the ETSU values. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education administration, student development, social work, counseling, or a related field and four (4) or more years of relevant experience at the professional, full-time level. OR Five years of work experience with a social services program. OR A combination of education and work experience. Successful completion of a background check required as a condition of employment. Preferred Qualifications Experience in residence life, residential education, housing operations, or student development within a higher education setting. Demonstrated ability to supervise professional staff and support their growth through coaching and feedback. Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Physical Demands (as needed) Sitting for extended periods (e.g., at a computer or workstation) Climbing stairs or ladders Reaching overhead or below waist level Carrying files, equipment, or supplies short distances Pushing or pulling carts, furniture, or equipment Frequent typing or keyboard use Visual acuity to read printed and electronic materials Hearing to distinguish sounds (e.g., phone calls, alarms) Speaking clearly in noisy environments Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Student Services Professional 3 Salary: Market Range 8 ( Salary Schedules ) For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1299": {
      "title": "Director, Center for Academic Achievement",
      "description": "Category: Student Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Director of the Center for Academic Achievement (CFAA) provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for a comprehensive portfolio of academic support programs and services designed to advance student success, retention. persistence, and graduation in alignment with the university's strategic priorities. The Center supports undergraduate and graduate students through services including on-site and online tutoring in writing, mathematics, science, general education, and select upper-level courses; Supplemental Instruction in high-impact and high-challenge courses; academic coaching; and proactive academic support for students identified through early-intervention processes, midterm grades, institutional data, and referrals from faculty and staff. The Director provides leadership and oversight for the Center's professional and student staff and is directly responsible for the supervision, development, and performance management of professional staff, including the Assistant Director and Office Coordinator. In collaboration with the Assistant Director. the Director ensures the effective development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of CFAA programs and services. The Director oversees the recruitment, training, supervision, and development structures supporting more than 100 graduate and undergraduate student employees and ensures the responsible stewardship of the Center's fiscal, human, and operational resources. Using assessment data, institutional metrics, student performance indicators, and emerging student needs, the Director works collaboratively with the Assistant Director and other CFAA staff to evaluate program effectiveness, identify opportunities for improvement, and establish strategic priorities for academic support. The Director partners with academic departments, faculty, advisors, and student success units to identify courses and student populations that would benefit from targeted academic interventions, including tutoring, Supplemental Instruction, academic coaching, workshops, and other academic support strategies. The Director serves as a university leader and subject-matter expert in academic support and student success, fostering strong partnerships with administrators, faculty, and staff across the institution. The Director represents the Center and university through campus committees, professional associations, conferences, and collaborative initiatives and promotes innovative, evidence-informed practices that strengthen student learning and academic achievement. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of academic support, student success, retention, persistence, and academic intervention practices in higher education. Knowledge of evidence-informed practices related to tutoring, Supplemental Instruction, academic coaching, and peer learning. Demonstrated leadership and supervisory skills, including professional staff development, performance management, and team building. Strong strategic planning, organizational management, and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and initiatives. Ability to use assessment data, institutional metrics, and student performance indicators to evaluate effectiveness and guide continuous improvement and KPI's for the center. Knowledge of fiscal and resource management, including budget development, resource allocation, and responsible stewardship. Ability to interpret institutional policies, exercise independent judgment, and effectively address complex or unique situations. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative partnerships with faculty, academic departments, administrators, and student support units. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills with the ability to communicate effectively with diverse university and external stakeholders. Required Qualifications Master's degree or higher in education, student affairs, English, learning support, or a related field. Three (3) years of leadership or supervisory experience in a higher education or comparable professional setting. Experience supervising a student employee workforce. Preferred Qualifications Experience managing tutoring, Supplemental Instruction, academic coaching, learning centers, writing centers, or similar academic support programs. Experience with program assessment, student success analytics, or other data-informed program improvement. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Student Services Management 2 Market Range: 9 ( Salary Schedules ) For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1235": {
      "title": "Fellowship Site Director",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: United States The ETSU Department of Internal Medicine is seeking qualified faculty members to serve as Site Director for various clinical rotation sites within the Department of Internal Medicine Fellowship Programs. The Site Director provides leadership and oversight of the fellowship educational experience at the participating clinical site and serves as a key liaison between the fellowship program, site faculty, and clinical leadership. This is a temporary, part-time appointment. Key Responsibilities Include: Provide leadership and oversight of the fellowship educational experience at the participating site. Provide and/or coordinate appropriate clinical supervision, teaching, mentorship, and evaluation of fellows. Monitor fellow clinical and educational experiences to ensure alignment with program goals, curriculum, and applicable accreditation requirements. Coordinate site-based educational activities and support meaningful clinical and scholarly learning opportunities. Provide timely, constructive feedback and communicate significant fellow performance or educational concerns to the Fellowship Program Director. Foster a professional learning environment that promotes clinical excellence, patient safety, quality improvement, professionalism, scholarly activity, and fellow well-being. Collaborate with fellowship leadership, faculty, and clinical leadership to support continuous improvement of the educational experience. Assist with program evaluation, accreditation activities, and compliance with applicable institutional and fellowship program requirements. About the Quillen College of Medicine: East Tennessee State University’s Quillen College of Medicine is nationally recognized for its commitment to primary care education and service to rural and underserved populations. In the 2025 U.S. News & World Report rankings, Quillen College of Medicine was named a Tier 1 medical school for Primary Care and ranked #2 in the nation for Most Graduates Practicing in Medically Underserved Areas. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of graduate medical education principles and fellowship program requirements. Knowledge of applicable accreditation standards, institutional policies, and requirements governing fellow education and supervision. Strong clinical knowledge and expertise within the applicable specialty or subspecialty. Ability to effectively teach, supervise, mentor, and evaluate fellows. Ability to assess learner performance and provide timely, constructive feedback. Strong organizational and administrative skills. Ability to develop and maintain effective educational processes and documentation. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and communication skills. Demonstrated clinical experience and expertise in the applicable specialty or subspecialty. Demonstrated experience in teaching, supervising, mentoring, or evaluating residents, fellows, medical students, or other healthcare learners. Ability to identify and address educational, performance, patient safety, and learning-environment concerns. Ability to collaborate effectively with program leadership, faculty, clinical staff, and institutional stakeholders. Commitment to professionalism, patient-centered care, quality improvement, patient safety, and fellow well-being. Required Qualifications: Doctor of Medicine (MD), Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO), or other degree appropriate to the specialty and institutional requirements. Current medical licensure and appropriate medical staff appointment in the jurisdiction in which the participating site is located, as applicable. Active faculty appointment with the Department of Internal Medicine Board certification in the applicable specialty or subspecialty Salary - $12,000 per year (temporary position-no benefits) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The posting is subject to change without notice to the applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter, CV and Copy of Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1279": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Economics and Finance",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The Department of Economics and Finance in the College of Business and Technology of East Tennessee State University in Johnson City, TN is seeking highly qualified individuals to serve as adjunct faculty to teach courses in economics, finance, and quantitative methods. A master's degree from an accredited university with eighteen credit hours in the discipline is preferred. Those applicants with extensive work experience in the field in lieu of discipline-specific academic preparation will also be considered and are strongly encouraged to apply. We expect day and evening times will be available beginning in January 2027. Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Three references are required along with the application, CV, cover letter, and a copy of transcripts. Reference letters can be sent directly to Taylor Stevenson, Ph.D., Chair, Economics and Finance, ETSU, Box 70686, Johnson City, TN 37614 (email: stevenst@etsu.edu ) ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. All applications and vitas must be submitted electronically at jobs.etsu.edu. In addition to the ETSU application, you will be required to provide the names and email addresses of 3 references. If your references are unable to use the electronic system, they may send the letter directly to Taylor Stevenson, Ph.D., Chair, Economics and Finance, ETSU, Box 70686, Johnson City, TN 37614 (email: stevenst@etsu.edu ) "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1282": {
      "title": "Senior Research Analyst",
      "description": "Category: Data Analytics JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Senior Research Analyst supports institutional decision-making by collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data related to student enrollment, retention, graduation, faculty workload, academic programs, and other key institutional measures. Reporting to the Director of Institutional Research, this role conducts research on higher education trends and issues, develops data dashboards and visualizations, and provides actionable insights to institutional leaders and stakeholders. The Senior Research Analyst collaborates with campus partners to identify research needs, design and conduct research projects, and perform statistical analyses using tools such as R. The position also supports institutional, state, and federal reporting requirements; accreditation efforts at the institution and program levels; and the preparation of reports and presentations for internal and external audiences. Additionally, the analyst contributes to the advancement of institutional research, planning, assessment, and effectiveness through professional presentations and publications while staying current with emerging trends and best practices in data analysis and higher education research. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Expertise in quantitative data analysis, including descriptive and inferential statistics, multivariate analysis, and predictive modeling. Proficiency in statistical software such as SPSS, SAS, and R. Experience developing data visualizations and dashboards using tools such as Tableau and Power BI. Strong ability to translate complex data and technical findings into clear, concise, and actionable information for non-technical audiences. Excellent analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and project management skills. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and manage multiple projects and priorities. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a relevant field such as statistics, social sciences, or higher education research with a minimum of 2 years of experience in institutional research or a related field OR an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of higher education data systems, institutional research practices, and state and federal reporting requirements. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Data Analyst 2 Market Range - 7 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions and additional details Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check Applications must include a cover letter, resume, and three (3) professional references ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employe r University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1245": {
      "title": "Professor of Pathology and Histology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Medical Education at the Quillen College of Medicine invites applications for a full-time tenure track or non-tenure track Professor of Pathology and Histology. This position supports the instructional mission of the College through teaching of pathology, histology, pathophysiology, medicine, and other clinical sciences to medical students, residents, and other health professions students. The successful candidate will contribute to medical education through active learning instruction, integrated medical curriculum delivery, medical education scholarship, and basic science and/or medical education-based research. The faculty member will also participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Responsibilities Include: Develop course objectives linked to USMLE content and QCOM institutional educational objectives where histology and pathology are relevant. Develop and deliver pathology, histology, and pathophysiology materials necessary for pre-clinical medical students. Teach pathology, histology, and pathophysiology content to medical students using active-learning and small-group facilitation. Write and modify quality NBME-style questions with faculty and staff support to be used in both the classroom and assessment settings, ensuring fair and accurate evaluation of student learning. Collaborate with faculty across basic and clinical sciences to ensure content integration. Act as a team-member to ensure courses and learning activities run smoothly. Work as a valued team-member in implementing course continuous quality improvement. Lead pathology specific didactic sessions to pathology residents. Integrate clinical correlations into the pre-clinical discipline specific instruction. Participate in curriculum development, implementation, and assessment. Conduct scholarly activities in basic sciences, clinical medicine, and/or medical education. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and ability to teach pathology and histology at the medical school level. Ability to lead pathology resident teaching activities. Ability to integrate clinical correlations into pre-clinical medical education. Ability to conduct scholarly research and mentor medical students in such endeavors. Strong communication, instructional, and mentoring skills. Ability to navigate and utilize educational-based software for educational purposes. Expertise and interest in molecular pathology, pediatric pathology, urologic pathology, GI pathology, and thoracic pathology. Clinical experience as a practicing pathologist. Demonstrated experience with administration of medical education. Experience in physician assistant education and training programming. Demonstrated experience teaching pathology related content to medical students. Required Qualifications Applicants must have: M.D. and Ph.D. degrees with expertise in experimental pathology. Board certification in both anatomic and clinical pathology. Full professor status at current institution. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching other health related content within an integrated medical school curriculum. Evidence of research and/or medical education scholarship. Experience mentoring medical, graduate or other professional students. Membership in professional pathology societies that are either regional or national Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary - Based on commensurate For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date is subject to change without notice to the applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Required documents to attach: Cover Letter, CV and Copy of Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1242": {
      "title": "Temporary Full-Time Research Technician",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Biomedical Sciences in the College of Medicine at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Research Technician for a Temporary Hourly Full-Time position. In this role, you will work closely with Dr. Valentin Yakubenko ( faculty webpage ), contributing to innovative biomedical research and supporting the laboratory’s ongoing research activities. You will become part of a research team investigating the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying inflammatory diseases, including sepsis and atherosclerosis. The research utilizes a variety of molecular biology, cell biology, and biochemical techniques, as well as mouse models of inflammatory diseases. This position involves performing a range of technical duties related to laboratory experiments, standardized assays, data collection, and general research support. Key Responsibilities: Perform technical duties of a physical or biological nature to support research activities, Assist with data collection, interpretation, evaluation, and documentation for lab projects, Operate and set up laboratory or research equipment for experiments, Collect, tabulate, and calculate data using various electronic devices, Maintain computer databases of research and protocol records, Order, replace, and maintain laboratory supplies, Conduct minor repairs on research equipment as needed, Perform general laboratory maintenance and cleanup, Train and supervise new research personnel, Occasional evening and weekend work may be required, Carry out additional duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Knowledge of basic laboratory methodology. Knowledge of business English and arithmetic. Ability to perform basic informational research projects. Ability to gather, compile, and analyze data. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues and the public. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office. Required Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience working in a biomedical laboratory. Important Notes: This position is based on-site and is not eligible for remote work. Please note that sponsorship is not available for this position. Compensation & Benefits: Salary: $­­20.00 per hour Benefits: ( Employee Benefits ) *This is an on-site position * This position does not have funding available for visa sponsorship. Application Requirements & Conditions: Attach the following documents: Cover Letter , Resume , and three (3) References that include a phone number and an e-mail address. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Employment is contingent upon approved work authorization. Employment is contingent upon sufficient grant funding. Non-Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1251": {
      "title": "Clinical Geneticist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary: East Tennessee State University Pediatrics Department seeks a well-qualified clinical geneticist. The academic rank will be determined by the education and experience of the candidate. This position is housed within the Department of Pediatrics; however, the position will work with a rapidly expanding health sciences center consisting of medicine, pharmacy, nursing, public health, allied health, and a large VA system. Other Considerations for this Position: Academic responsibilities include teaching of medical students and pediatric residents as well as academic and scholarly pursuits. Expansion of the clinical genetics program. Opportunities for research. Create new models of care to serve a large rural service area in collaboration with mid-level practitioners, pediatricians, other primary care providers, and specialists. Provide clinical services for genetics patients. Participation in the regional state newborn screening program. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach medical students and residents. Ability to perform routine inpatient and outpatient genetic patients. Create new models of care to serve a large rural service area. Provide clinical services for pediatrics, oncology, obstetrics and gynecology, psychiatry, internal medicine, surgery, and family medicine. Required Qualifications: MD/DO Completion of genetics fellowship at time of hire. Must be BC/BE in genetics at time of hire. Benefits and Compensation: Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with experience. For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) *J1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply. *Position is contingent upon sufficient funding. Application Instructions: Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Required documents to attach: Cover Letter, CV, and Copy of Transcripts. About the Region: ETSU is nestled in the foothills of the scenic Appalachian Highlands, Johnson City, TN combines big city amenities, small town charm, and world class outdoor recreation with living costs well below the national average. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodation s. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1253": {
      "title": "Academic Hospitalist-Internal Medicine",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary The ETSU Department of Internal Medicine invites board-certified or board-eligible Internists to join our established inpatient hospitalist team. Whether your passion lies in teaching, clinical care, research, or leadership, your career will be supported and encouraged within our collaborative academic environment. Key Responsibilities Include: Diagnose, treat, and manage hospitalized patients Mentor and teach medical students and residents during inpatient rotations Conduct lectures, lead case discussions, and provide hands-on clinical training Contribute to the advancement of internal medicine through education, quality improvement, and scholarly activity Internal Medicine faculty members benefit from the guidance of experienced academic leaders and a supportive environment that fosters professional development and growth. Compensation aligns with AAMC salary recommendation benchmarks for each specialty. About the Quillen College of Medicine: East Tennessee State University’s Quillen College of Medicine is nationally recognized for its commitment to primary care education and service to rural and underserved populations. In the 2025 U.S. News & World Report rankings, Quillen was named a Tier 1 medical school for Primary Care and ranked #2 in the nation for Most Graduates Practicing in Medically Underserved Areas. These honors reflect our enduring mission to prepare compassionate physicians dedicated to meeting the needs of all communities. If you are a dedicated Internist seeking to make a meaningful impact in a supportive and mission-driven academic setting, we encourage you to apply and become a valued member of our team. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Comprehensive knowledge of inpatient internal medicine and evidence-based clinical practice. Skilled in teaching, mentoring, and evaluating medical students and residents. Strong interpersonal and communication skills for effective collaboration with multidisciplinary teams. Proficiency in electronic health record documentation and clinical workflow optimization. Commitment to professionalism, ethical practice, and patient-centered care. Ability to balance clinical duties with educational and scholarly responsibilities. Capacity to contribute to academic initiatives, including research, quality projects, or committee service. Required Qualifications Medical Degree (MD or DO) from an accredited institution Successful completion of Internal Medicine residency program from an ACGME-accredited program Board Certified or Board Eligible at time of interview Preferred Qualifications Experience in medical education Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary - $100,000 For information on benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: CV, Cover Letter, and Copy of Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
