    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1278": {
      "title": "Production Coordinator",
      "description": "Category: Operations JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary The Production Coordinator operates a variety of production and bindery equipment and provides mechanical production support to produce and deliver high-quality finished products. Verifies product specifications and utilizes cost-effective production methods as directed. Coordinates with the departmental team to meet production demands using the BMC website and custom ordering and workflow systems. Performs routine equipment maintenance and communicates equipment repair or maintenance needs to the Production Director. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and experience in print production operations, including prepress, offset printing, digital printing, wide-format printing, and associated technical protocols. Comprehensive knowledge of methods and techniques used to produce high-quality printed materials, displays, signage, and promotional products. Knowledge of color management systems, including digital file preparation requirements for offset and digital printing, color profiling using a spectrophotometer, registration methods, bindery techniques, and paper stocks. Operational knowledge of finishing and bindery equipment, processes, and techniques. Knowledge of print production planning, scheduling, and workflow coordination to meet customer demand and project deadlines. Knowledge of estimating job costs, supplies, materials, and other production resources, including cost-control, quality-control, and logistical considerations. Ability to safely operate, maintain, troubleshoot, and perform routine repairs on production equipment. Ability to instruct and oversee others in the safe operation of production equipment, including equipment that may present safety hazards. Knowledge of Mac and PC platforms, graphics processes, and relevant software, including EFI Fiery, FusionPro, Adobe Creative Cloud, and Microsoft Office, as well as associated peripherals such as scanners and wide-format printers. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret technical information related to high-end graphics software, raster image processing (RIP) software, production equipment, and hardware. Ability to understand and effectively utilize online traffic, ordering, and production workflow systems. Ability to exercise sound judgment in determining appropriate strategies and methods for project development and production. Ability to exercise sound judgment and adhere to ETSU policies and procedures when coordinating supply purchases and outsourced printing services. Ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize competing demands, and consistently meet production deadlines. Required Qualifications Associate’s degree and three (3) years of experience in progressively responsible roles within the printing industry OR A combination of education and work experience Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Extensive customer service experience demonstrating the ability to manage client relationships and expectations. Experience with digital media desired, and its integration into print and cross-platform projects. Proven ability to successfully execute projects across multiple media formats with adaptability and precision. Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Operations Specialist 3 Salary – MR 4 ($36,809.75 - $49,693.16) For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to the applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter and Resume *This is an on-site position * This position does not have funding available for visa sponsorship. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
