    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1261": {
      "title": "Grounds Foreman",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Employees in this classification work under general supervision and perform a variety of skilled tasks related to grounds maintenance, landscaping, gardening, turf care, and related activities. Work includes the use and maintenance of hand tools, power equipment, and other grounds maintenance equipment, as well as instructing other employees. Employees exercise independent judgment in determining appropriate methods for completing assigned work and perform related duties as required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of methods, materials, tools, equipment, and practices used in grounds maintenance and landscaping Knowledge of basic landscaping, gardening, and turf maintenance procedures Knowledge of materials, supplies, and equipment used in turf and grounds maintenance Knowledge of proper pesticide application methods and safety practices Ability to direct, instruct, and supervise the work of other employees Ability to properly use, operate, and maintain a variety of hand tools, power tools, machinery, and related equipment Ability to follow oral and written instructions and established procedures Ability to exercise sound judgment and determine appropriate methods for completing assigned work Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with supervisors, coworkers, and other employees Ability to perform pesticide applications in accordance with established procedures and applicable requirements Ability to perform heavy manual labor for extended periods of time and work outdoors under varying weather conditions Ability to work independently and effectively prioritize and complete assigned tasks Required Qualifications Successful completion of the tenth (10th) grade. Experience in grounds maintenance, gardening, landscaping, turf care, or a related field. Must possess and maintain a valid Tennessee driver's license. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of experience in grounds maintenance, gardening, landscaping, turf care, or a related field. High school diploma or GED. Experience directing, instructing, or supervising employees. Experience operating and maintaining grounds maintenance equipment Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services Buildings and Grounds Assistant 2 Market Range - 3 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions and additional details Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Cover letter, resume, and three references available upon request. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1274": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Communication Studies and Storytelling at East Tennessee State University seeks an Associate Professor of Communication Studies. This position carries full-time, tenure-track status beginning August 15, 2027, as an academic year appointment pending continued availability of funds. We seek a colleague with a demonstrated emphasis in Organizational Communication, and a record of teaching, service, and research appropriate for the rank of Associate Professor. We are especially interested in candidates who have a secondary interest in one or more of the following areas: Crisis and Risk Communication, Social Media & Digital Communication, Applied Communication, or Political Communication. We are open to candidates who use any Communication Studies research methodology. Our new colleague must demonstrate respect and value for the use of narrative and storytelling in teaching and scholarship, although their research may or may not incorporate narrative. Teaching (60%)—The expected teaching load is a 3/3. This faculty member will primarily teach in our undergraduate Communication Studies major and minor programs but may have opportunities to teach graduate courses for our Graduate Certificate in Storytelling. They will be expected to teach existing undergraduate courses in Organizational Communication, Business and Professional Communication, and Communicating in Groups. The successful candidate will also have the ability to teach one or more of the following undergraduate courses currently in our catalog: Communication Theory, Professional Communication & Technology, Advanced Public Speaking, Speaking for Social Change, and/or Communication Ethics. We are especially interested in candidates who are willing to develop new courses in Organizational Communication and at least one of the following areas: Crisis and Risk Communication, Social Media and Digital Communication, Applied Communication, and/or Political Communication. Our new colleague will serve on undergraduate honors thesis committees and hold regular oﬃce hours for students. Teaching formats may include in-person, hybrid, and online teaching. Summer and winter teaching opportunities are optional and available depending on need. The successful candidate must demonstrate a record of teaching in breadth and quality that is commensurate with the rank of Associate Professor. We are especially interested in candidates interested or experienced in community-engaged learning. Service (20%)—Applicants should make clear their ability to step into service obligations expected of an Associate Professor. Service duties will include coordinating our undergraduate internship program and potentially growing and supporting our undergraduate Communication Studies Association and/or coordinating the teaching of one of our oral communication general education courses. All faculty advise undergraduate students on their program of study. We are particularly interested in candidates who have strong organizational skills, demonstrated ability to work in collegial and collaborative environments, and experience in community-engaged work. In addition to the duties described above, tenure-track faculty members contribute professional service to the college, university, discipline, and/or community. Research & Creative Activity (20%)—Tenure-track faculty contribute to the mission of the Department of Communication Studies & Storytelling through a program of research and/or creative activity that leads to publication, peer-reviewed performances, and/or competitively selected performances. Applicants must show how their existing record of scholarship is consistent with the university’s expectations for the rank of Associate Professor. The Department of Communication Studies & Storytelling serves just over 90 majors and minors at the undergraduate level, as well as hundreds of students enrolled in general education courses in oral communication. The award-winning ETSU Speech & Debate Team and the Storyteller Collective are also housed within the department. The department currently has 12 full-time faculty members with areas of expertise across communication and storytelling fields. Required Qualifications Candidates must have a Ph.D. or terminal degree in communication studies or other related field. Emphasis in Organizational Communication A record of teaching breadth and quality appropriate to the rank of Associate Professor. A record of peer-reviewed publication or performance and/or grant-funded research appropriate for the rank of Associate Professor. A record of service to academic departments, college, university, discipline, and/or community commensurate with the rank of Associate Professor. Secondary specialization or interest in one or more of the following: Crisis and risk communication Social Media and Digital Communication Applied Communication Political Communication Preferred Qualifications Interest or experience in directing a Communication Studies internship program Interest or experience in community-engaged work and/or teaching Compensation & Benefits Salary - $67,000 For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Applicant review will begin on October 5, 2026 and we will be accepting applications until October 15, 2026. Please include the following items in your application: Curriculum vitae Minimum 3 professional references on your CV who will submit letters of recommendation by October 15 th Cover letter that specifically addresses the job summary and the required and preferred qualifications listed in this posting Evidence of teaching excellence and demonstration of breadth of teaching experience (e.g., type of course, level of instruction, and frequency) 1–2-page research and/or creative activity agenda and 1-2 page document that speaks to the quality of the applicant’s scholarship as appropriate for Associate Professor status; 1-2 page document describing the applicant’s history and quality of service at previous institutions; Transcripts must be submitted to be considered for review; unoﬃcial transcripts or a copy of the transcript is acceptable for application purposes. Oﬃcial transcripts may be required upon hire. ABD candidates should provide documentation in the application materials that the Ph.D. degree will be conferred prior to August 15, 2027. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer : The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1141": {
      "title": "Part-time Dental Hygiene Adjunct Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU Dental Hygiene Program is seeking registered dental hygienists to provide clinical instruction to dental hygiene students. Openings are available for the days/times listed below: Monday 8:00-12:15 Tuesday 8:00-12:15 Wednesday 8:00-12:15 Thursday 8:00-12:15 Friday 8:00-12:15 Employment is contingent upon student enrollment, program needs, and applicant’s availability on scheduled clinic days each semester. Program needs may vary each semester, so employment is not guaranteed each semester. This posting may remain open to retain a pool of instructors. Job Responsibilities Clinical instruction and supervision for first- and second-year dental hygiene students Participation in faculty meetings and calibration sessions. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in dental hygiene or a related field Graduate of an ADA-accredited dental hygiene program Must be currently licensed to practice dental hygiene in the state of Tennessee (or eligible for licensure) Minimum of five years of clinical dental hygiene experience Current CPR certification Willingness to complete continuing education courses in educational methodology Preferred Qualifications Local anesthesia certification Experience with Patterson Eaglesoft Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a successful background check. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1224": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Category: Research and Labs JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary ETSU Quillen College of Medicine, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases, invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate to participate in innovative translational research focused on human viral immunology. The Division offers a thriving academic research environment with outstanding facilities, diverse patient resources, and access to NIH, VA, and Department of Defense-supported research programs. The Postdoctoral Research Associate will work closely with physician-scientists and research faculty within the Division of Infectious Diseases to investigate mechanisms of viral infection, immune response, inflammation, aging, and immune dysfunction. The position will also provide opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration with faculty and investigators within the Center for Inflammation, Infectious Diseases and Immunology (CIIDI) at Quillen College of Medicine. Candidates with research experience or demonstrated interest in one or more of the following areas are particularly encouraged to apply: T-cell biology and T-cell aging Telomere biology HIV and other viral infections Inflammaging and cellular senescence DNA damage and repair signaling pathways Exosome biology and extracellular vesicle signaling miRNA regulation Myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) development and function T follicular helper (TFH) and T helper (TH) cell differentiation Human viral immunology and translational immunology Key Responsibilities: Conduct laboratory and/or translational research under the direction of faculty mentors. Assist with the design, execution, analysis, and interpretation of research studies. Apply appropriate molecular, cellular, immunologic, and/or virologic techniques to research projects. Analyze and interpret experimental data using appropriate scientific methods. Maintain accurate research records and documentation. Present research findings at departmental, institutional, and professional meetings. Prepare manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, and other scholarly materials. Collaborate with physician-scientists, research faculty, trainees, and multidisciplinary investigators. Participate in research activities and professional development opportunities through the Division of Infectious Diseases and CIIDI. Contribute to the development of research projects and pursue opportunities for scholarly publications Demonstrated research experience through doctoral training, publications, presentations, or other scholarly activities. Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Minimum Requirements: PhD, MD, MD/PhD, or equivalent doctoral degree in immunology, microbiology, virology, molecular biology, biomedical sciences, or a closely related field. Viral immunology research experience is required, HIV/HCV infection is preferred Research Environment: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will be part of a collaborative research environment within the Division of Infectious Diseases and CIIDI, with opportunities to interact with investigators across Quillen College of Medicine. The position provides access to clinical and translational research resources and opportunities to participate in NIH, VA, and DoD-supported research initiatives. This is an excellent opportunity for a motivated postdoctoral researcher seeking to advance expertise in human viral immunology, immunosenescence, inflammation, and translational infectious disease research while working alongside established physician-scientists and multidisciplinary investigators. Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Researcher 2 Salary – MR 6 For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The posting is subject to change without notice to the applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please include the following documents: Cover Letter and Resume ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodation s. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1225": {
      "title": "Temporary Technical - Production Assistant",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: United States Production Assistant Classification: Temporary/Part-Time Schedule: Averaging 15-20 hours per week, with potential for more hours based upon project load. Department: Biomedical Communications – 31130 Job Summary Responsible to the Director of Production at BMC Creative, assisting with University production services, print operations, and serving a university-wide customer base that extends to ETSU Health clinical locations and administrative offices. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and experience of print operations, including prepress, offset printing, wide-format, and digital press technical protocols. Operational knowledge and understanding of finishing equipment and processes. Knowledge of press schedules to meet customer demand. Understanding of color management systems with practical experience to include digital file preparation requirements for offset printing and digital prepress, bindery techniques, and paper stocks; with color profiling using a spectrophotometer; and of methods for gaining optimal registration. Knowledge of computers, both Mac and PC platforms, and current graphics processes and proprietary software, including EFI Fiery, Fusion Pro, Adobe Creative Cloud, and Microsoft Office, to include the operation of associated peripherals such as flatbed and transparency scanners and high-end, wide-format poster printers. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret technical information related to the use of high-end computer graphics software, RIP software, and hardware. Able to safely use production equipment, which may be hazardous. Able to safely maintain production equipment, including equipment repairs. Ability to understand and utilize online traffic systems. Ability to handle multiple projects and meet deadlines. Extensive customer service experience demonstrating the ability to manage client relationships and expectations. Experience with digital media is desired, and its integration into print and cross-platform projects. Proven ability to successfully execute projects across multiple media formats with adaptability and precision. Ability to provide support under physical demand, such as lifting/carrying up to 50 lbs. Ability to transport and deliver, to and from academic and clinical campuses, and various businesses Required Qualifications Associate or Bachelor’s degree desired, preferably in Print Technology, Graphic Imaging, Industrial Management, or a related field with relevant professional experience. Minimum of one (1) year of experience in progressively responsible roles within the printing industry. Must have reliable transportation and a valid driver’s license. Compensation and Benefits Salary - $18 -$20 an hour Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a successful background check. Please attach the following: Cover Letter and Resume. *This is an onsite position *Please note that this position does not have funding available for visa sponsorship . ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1256": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Math Education",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Early Childhood and Elementary Education at East Tennessee State University seeks a 9-month, tenure track Assistant Professor of Math Education position beginning August 2027 to teach in-person, online, and/or hybrid courses on the main campus in Johnson City and at the ETSU-Sevierville campus in teacher educator programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful applicant will teach undergraduate mathematics methods courses in the elementary education program which has seen a 25% increase in enrollment over the past two years. At the graduate level, the successful applicant may teach in the Master of Arts in Teaching and/or Master of Education in Curriculum and Instruction programs, both of which have experienced over a 30% increase in enrollment in the past year. In addition to teaching, candidates are expected to engage in research and scholarly activities and in service to the department, college, university, and profession. The typical annual workload is 60% teaching, 20% research, and 20% service. The successful applicant may also supervise teacher candidates in the field. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Ability and willingness to teach face-to-face, online, and hybrid courses at two locations. Willingness to engage with institutional student success initiatives. Hold a commitment to engaging with best practice initiatives in instruction and pedagogy, mentoring, and curriculum design and development. Demonstrated commitment to advancing a strong and growing research and scholarship agenda appropriate to the mathematics education discipline. Ability to work with diverse populations and perspectives of students, faculty, and staff in support of the college’s and university’s mission. Required Qualifications Earned terminal degree (EdD or PhD) in Mathematics Education, Elementary Education, Curriculum and Instruction, or similar field with a concentration in math or STEM; ABD will be considered with degree awarded by August 13, 2027 Minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in mathematics or mathematics education courses Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching mathematics in grades K-8, especially K-5, in a U.S. school setting Experience supervising and/or mentoring pre-service student teacher candidates, especially in K-5 field placements Experience teaching face-to-face and online education courses, especially in mathematics education, at the university level Experience developing online education courses, especially mathematics education courses, at the university level Demonstrated potential to secure external research funding Compensation & Benefits Salary commensurate with experience. For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter CV Transcripts (or documentation of current degree status) Recommendation Letters/References ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/797": {
      "title": "Graduate Nursing PMHNP Faculty (Non-Tenure, 12-Month Appointment)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU College of Nursing, Department of Graduate Nursing Programs, invites applications for a 12-month, open-rank, tenured/tenure-track faculty position. Successful candidates will be expected to contribute primarily to teaching in the graduate nursing program. However, the incumbent should have the ability to contribute to the College’s teaching, research, and service responsibilities across undergraduate and graduate programs. The position requires engagement in classroom, lab, simulation, and clinical-based teaching, supporting the development of future nursing professionals. The new faculty will join a dynamic group of nursing educators with a strong commitment to student success through innovative evidence-based teaching strategies, inter-professional collaboration, and fostering an environment where every student feels valued and supported. Candidates should have the scholarly preparation expected of faculty in research academic environments. Candidates should show evidence of strong teaching ability at the collegiate level, a record of peer-reviewed scholarly productivity appropriate to rank, and the potential – or, if at the Associate level, a documented history - of securing external funding. They must maintain an active, clearly defined program of research that aligns with and advances the mission and vision of the ETSU College of Nursing, particularly its commitments to rural health, community engagement, and improving health outcomes in the Appalachian region. This position requires teaching, research and service duties to be conducted in person on campus. Remote or hybrid work options are not available. Rank is determined at the time of hiring. Candidates considered for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor must possess a terminal academic doctoral degree in nursing or related field by the start date and demonstrate the potential for research productivity. Some appointments may be eligible for tenure. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of computer/audiovisual software and technology, including learning management systems and supplemental instructional platforms. Knowledge of evidence-based nursing education practices. Knowledge of nursing accreditation standards. Knowledge of current healthcare practices including current technologies. Ability to communicate effectively, orally and in writing, with a wide range of faculty, staff, students, and clinical partners. Ability to effectively engage and motivate students. Ability to work collaboratively with administration, faculty, staff, and clinical partners. Ability to engage in clinical teaching as per workload assignment. Ability to travel to clinical agencies based on workload assignment. Ability to travel to other campus sites for teaching as per workload negotiation. All applicants must demonstrate the ability to communicate effectively in written and spoken English in accordance with the Tennessee Board of Regents policy 5:02:01:03. Required Qualifications DNP or PhD in Nursing (exceptional candidates completing their PhD may be considered but must be awarded prior to the hire date). If PhD is not in Nursing, then candidates must hold an MSN. Active/unencumbered RN licensure in the State of Tennessee or compact/multistate required by the date of hire. Preferred Qualifications Greater than or equal to five (5) years’ experience in higher education. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by the employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job across various settings in the classroom, simulation, clinical, and/or community. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, climb, reach, and balance. The employee may occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, and/or move more than 100 pounds. The employee must be able to perceive and respond to sounds and alarms; communicate effectively with others; and have a sufficient vision regarding near, distance, color, peripheral, and depth perception as well as the ability to observe and monitor situations in full and dimmed light. The employee may stand, walk, and/or sit in various settings for up to 12 hours at a time in addition to the preparation and closure of a clinical shift. Rapid mobility may also be required on occasion. Physical expectations of an assigned clinical facility may vary and be subject to change. Stress levels may be high due to frequently dealing with numerous students, patients, family members, and other healthcare providers. This position demands concentration and the ability to work in emotionally-charged situations. Compensation & Benefits Salary and rank commensurate with education and experience. For information on benefits please visit: www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume Copy of current/active RN licensure in the State of Tennessee or compact/multistate. An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. College of Nursing Overview The College of Nursing is part of the University’s Academic Health Sciences Center, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is the largest in the State of Tennessee offering multiple tracks for students enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs. The Department of Undergraduate Programs is home to over 45 full-time faculty and 700 students across five (5) tracks including the Traditional BSN, Accelerated BSN (Johnson City, Kingsport, Sevierville), LPN-BSN, and RN-BSN/Dual Degree. The Department of Undergraduate Programs boasts a record of excellence with 60% of faculty holding specialty certifications and a strong record of collaboration and successful student outcomes. All programs in the College of Nursing are fully accredited by the CCNE. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1142": {
      "title": "PRN Supervising Dentist for Dental Hygiene Program",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The ETSU Dental Hygiene Program is seeking a PRN dentist to provide clinical instruction and supervision of dental hygiene students in the Dental Hygiene Clinic. Responsibilities include clinical supervision reviewing patient medical histories evaluating student assessments of new patients supervising local anesthesia injections evaluating radiographs evaluating pathology discussing the need for referral with patients serving as a dental and medical resource for students and dental hygiene faculty and taking the lead in the event of a medical emergency supervising sealant placement and occlusal adjustments assisting students with nightguards, etc. Required Qualifications Must be a licensed dentist in the state of Tennessee Current CPR Healthcare Provider certification Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff and patients with diverse backgrounds Employment is contingent upon student enrollment, program needs, and applicant’s availability on scheduled clinic days each semester. Program needs may vary each semester, so employment is not guaranteed each semester. This posting may remain open to retain a pool of instructors. Compensation Salary - $75.00 per hour For information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Position is contingent on a satisfactory background check Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter, Resume, and Copy of certifications ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodation s. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1244": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Management - Hospitality and Tourism Management",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Management and Supply Chain at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) in Johnson City, Tennessee, invites applications for a 9-month academic, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Management (Hospitality & Tourism Management). The position may begin in Spring 2027 or Fall 2027, depending on candidate availability and departmental needs. The successful candidate will support program needs at ETSU's main campus in Johnson City and may also teach or provide support at the Sevierville Center. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to teach, conduct high-quality research, and actively engage in institutional, professional, and community service activities, including student recruitment and continuous program improvement. We welcome candidates who are committed to building strong community relationships that support student success and provide valuable opportunities for experiential learning and career development. Review of applications will continue until a candidate is selected and recommended for appointment. To be considered for this position, applicants must complete an online application and submit the requested items. The College of Business and Technology at East Tennessee State University is AACSB accredited. CBAT employs approximately 100 full-time faculty members and serves over 3,000 students. Undergraduate concentrations are offered in accounting, computing, digital media, economics and finance, management, marketing, media and communications, military science, sports and recreation management, supply chain, as well as master’s degrees in accountancy, brand strategy, business administration, digital marketing, and digital media. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to develop and maintain a high-quality research agenda. Ability to teach both online and in-person. Ability to collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to enhance student learning and support departmental, programmatic, and college-wide initiatives. Ability to teach hospitality and tourism management courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels Ability to produce high-quality publications relevant to their courses and the strategic goals of the college (i.e., also an AACSB requirement). Knowledge and ability to use technology in various teaching modalities. Commitment to serving the university, college, department, and the professional community. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. or DBA in Hospitality and Tourism Management, Management, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution (or equivalent). Preferred Qualifications A strong record of scholarly research, demonstrated by publications in high-quality academic journals (e.g., those listed on the ABDC journal list) and evidence of an active research agenda. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching management courses at undergraduate and graduate levels, with experience in curriculum development or improvement. Experience integrating emerging technologies (e.g., AI, simulation platforms) into teaching and learning environments. Relevant professional or industry experience in hospitality and tourism management. Experience contributing to program innovation or interdisciplinary collaborations. Compensation & Benefits Salary dependent on qualifications. For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Additional Documents to Attach: CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodation s. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1203": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Political Science and Coordinator, Masters of Public Administration Program",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Political Science at East Tennessee State University invites applications for a tenure-track appointment at the level of associate professor beginning August 15, 2027. We are seeking a Coordinator of our Master’s in Public Administration Program and a candidate that can offer classes throughout Public Administration Core of our online MPA with particular interests in Nonprofit Management and Public Finance. The position is a 12-month faculty appointment which normally carries a 2/2 teaching load and comes with generous startup funding designed to promote a promising research agenda leading to peer reviewed publication. We are seeking a program leader with experience in earning NASPAA accreditation. Additionally, candidates must also be capable of excellent teaching in online graduate courses and in person sections of introduction to public administration. Service to the department, university, profession and community are also expected. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with securing NASPAA program accreditation. The ability and expertise to teach in the online MPA program. The ability to teach in the undergraduate political science program when necessary. Advising students and representing the department on university and college committees is also expected. Excellent oral and written communication skills are required. Required Qualifications Experience with NASPAA program accreditation. PhD in Public Administration, Political Science, or a related discipline, with ability to teach in the online MPA program as described. Evidence of original manuscript publication. Preferred Qualifications PhD subfields and teaching experience in Public Administration with concentration specialties in at least two the following: Local Government Management, Nonprofit Management, and Public Finance. Experience teaching online graduate courses in Public Administration. Experience teaching on ground undergraduate courses in Public Administration. Evidence of recent publication in the discipline. Compensation and Benefits Salary - $90,000 Startup funding- $5,000 Benefits – please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/. Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following: Cover Letter, CV, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, Declaration of Research Agenda, One-Page Description of Experience with NASPAA Accreditation, and Contact Information for Three References. If you have any questions, please reach out to Dr. Colin Glennon at glennon@etsu.edu. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students enrolled in highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1205": {
      "title": "Artist in Residence",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary The Department of Appalachian Studies at East Tennessee State University invites applications for an Artist in Residence in Bluegrass, Old-Time, and Roots Music Studies, to begin in August 2027. This is a full-time, non-tenure track position appointed on the basis of outstanding professional attainments, creative accomplishments, and recognition in the bluegrass and roots music entertainment field. The appointment is for one academic year (Aug. 15-May 15), with possible renewal for one year. Total compensation includes a full benefits package and salary of $69,500. The primary duties of the Artist in Residence are to produce and share live and/or recorded musical work, mentor students in private instruction and collaboration, and promote the Bluegrass, Old-Time, and Roots Music Program throughout the duration of employment. Artists in Residence have access to program resources including performance and recording spaces, the Archives of Appalachia, and dedicated teaching areas. Activities may include a performance residency, workshops or masterclasses, band leadership and mentorship, public lectures or performances, publications, and course development or instruction in the candidate’s area of expertise. The position requires campus presence when classes are in session, while allowing flexibility for an active touring schedule. Program and Institutional Context ETSU is located in northeast Tennessee near Bristol, Asheville, and the Carter Fold, offering students access to a vibrant regional network of festivals, venues, and traditional music communities in the heart of Appalachia. The university has become a recognized hub for the study and performance of American roots music, supported by the Department of Appalachian Studies and the Archives of Appalachia. The Bluegrass, Old-Time, and Roots Music program was founded by Jack Tottle in 1982 and is widely regarded as the oldest established program of its kind at any four-year institution. Building on that early vision, the program launched the world’s first baccalaureate degree in Bluegrass, Old-Time, and Country Music Studies in 2010, and now offers multiple concentrations and minors that prepare students for professional careers in performance, audio production, and related fields. The Department of Appalachian Studies includes undergraduate and graduate programs in Appalachian Studies, Scottish and Irish Studies, and related areas. It also includes the Center of Excellence in Appalachian Studies and Services, the Regional Resources Institute, the Reece Museum, and the Archives of Appalachia. This position supports ETSU’s mission to honor and preserve the heritage of Southern Appalachia through education, research, and service, and reflects the department’s goal of balancing academic and professional preparation. All positions are contingent upon sufficient funding, and ETSU states its commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Professional-level musical ability and experience. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Up-to-date and experiential knowledge of the bluegrass and roots music industry. Ability to promote the program to a wide range of audiences. Ability to collaborate with students to create musical work. Ability to help prepare students for careers as bluegrass or roots music professionals. Commitment to fostering a collegial learning environment in which equity, inclusion, and innovation are encouraged. Required Qualifications Professional bluegrass, old-time, or roots music performing artist with outstanding professional attainments, creative accomplishments, and recognition in the fields. Preferred Qualifications Top-level industry involvement and accomplishment as demonstrated by award nominations, artistic collaborations, noteworthy performances, broad fanbases, recordings, publications, instructional materials, or other accomplishments. Previous teaching experience, whether in a private studio or at an institution, is a plus. Application Instructions Applicants must complete the online application, including a cover letter, curriculum vitae, three professional references, and unofficial academic transcripts if applicable. Each applicant must also submit: Three professional audio recordings. Two live video performances. Optional additional materials include: A sample live instructional video. A sample of written instructional material. A brief statement of teaching philosophy. Videos, recordings, and instructional samples may be uploaded to Voyager or emailed to boner@etsu.edu. For large files, internet links such as YouTube are preferred. Contact Name: Dan Boner Contact Email: boner@etsu.edu Campus Box Number: 70435 Compensation & Benefits Salary: $69,500 For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1207": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary: The Doctor of Occupational Therapy Program in the Department of Rehabilitation is seeking one new faculty member for a 12-month clinical or tenure-track appointment to teach in the OTD program. The successful candidate is expected to participate as a full faculty member with all relevant duties, responsibilities, and benefits. The faculty member in this position is responsible for teaching in the area of content expertise (neuroscience, pathophysiology, neurological dysfunction) to assist occupational therapy students with knowledge acquisition and knowledge application necessary for entry-level practice in accordance with the accreditation standards and curriculum. The faculty member engages in service, scholarly activity, and supports the mission and vision of the university, department, and program. Candidates considered for a tenure-track position must possess a terminal academic doctoral degree by the start date and demonstrate the potential for research productivity. Faculty rank is commensurate with education and experience. Some appointments may be eligible for tenure. The Department of Rehabilitation is a growing multidisciplinary department with over 22 faculty and staff offering graduate programs in a Doctorate in Occupational Therapy, Doctorate in Physical Therapy, and a Master of Science in Orthotics and Prosthetics. The department is located within the College of Health Sciences, which includes numerous programs, including Speech and Language Pathology, Audiology, Social Work, and Allied Health Sciences. The College is part of the University's Academic Health Sciences Division, which also houses the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Nursing. The new faculty will join a dynamic and growing department focused on interprofessional education and training for the next generation of scholar-practitioners. East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution's focus on community engagement. The value of employment at ETSU goes far beyond salary. Regularly benefited ETSU employees enjoy a full range of benefits, services, and programs, including paid time off & leave, paid holidays, health and life insurance, retirement, access to university facilities and services, and much more! Check out the ETSU Human Resources Benefits page for additional information. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong commitment to graduate interprofessional education Knowledge of current trends and evidence-based practice in OT Knowledge of instructional strategies, to include online teaching experience Required Qualifications: Earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution (i.e., entry-level or post-professional clinical doctorate, PhD, EdD, ScD) Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in Tennessee Minimum of five years of full-time clinical experience Content expertise in neuroscience/neuroanatomy, pathophysiology, and neurological disorders Preferred Qualifications: Possess extensive teaching, clinical, and research experience in occupational therapy Terminal academic degree (EdD, PhD, ScD) Proven track record in scholarly activity Knowledge of ACOTE education standards and accreditation on-site process Experience in delivering online education Advanced clinical and teaching expertise in neuroscience and neurological disorders Minimum of 1 year of doctoral-level OT teaching experience and new program/curricular development Compensation & Benefits Salary commensurate with experience For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions and additional details Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Cover letter, CV, and three references available upon request. Copies of transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
