    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1230": {
      "title": "Chief Marketing and Communications Officer",
      "description": "Category: Communications and Marketing JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Guided by East Tennessee State University's mission and core values, the Chief Marketing and Communications Officer (CMCO) serves as the institution's senior communications strategist and brand leader. As a member of the University's leadership team, the CMCO advances ETSU's strategic priorities by developing and leading an integrated marketing, communications, and brand strategy that aligns with the University's vision, mission, and goals. The CMCO is responsible for elevating the visibility and reputation of the University through compelling storytelling, strategic communications, and effective brand stewardship. In partnership with campus leadership, the CMCO supports efforts to attract and retain students, engage alumni and donors, recruit outstanding faculty and staff, and strengthen relationships with community, governmental, and policy leaders. The CMCO also provides leadership during opportunities and challenges affecting the institution's public profile, ensuring consistent and effective communication across audiences and channels. The CMCO oversees the Office of University Marketing and Communications, leading a team of marketing and communications professionals responsible for advancing the University's goals through integrated communications, media relations, digital strategy, content development, and brand management. Beyond the central communications function, the CMCO provides strategic leadership and coordination for marketing and communications activities across the institution, fostering collaboration, consistency, and alignment among academic and administrative units. In carrying out these responsibilities, the CMCO models and advances ETSU's core values, fostering a culture where people are treated with dignity and respect, relationships are grounded in trust and integrity, diverse perspectives are valued, excellence is achieved through collaboration and innovation, resources are stewarded responsibly, and a commitment to intellectual achievement remains central to the University's mission. *PLEASE APPLY DIRECTLY AT THE LINK BELOW: https://wittkieffer.com/positions/a1wun0000024ufbmaq Knowledge, Skills and Abilities ▪ Demonstrated ability to develop and lead a strategic vision for the University’s marketing and communications efforts. ▪ Experience developing and leading strategic, data-driven, comprehensive marketing and communications campaigns involving a wide range of stakeholders. ▪ Exceptional management and coordination experience resulting in unified marketing and communications efforts and collaboration across campus units. ▪ Exceptional research and analytical skills with experience in measuring the effectiveness of marketing and communications initiatives. ▪ Demonstrated success in applying a broad range of communication tools, including marketing, public relations, copywriting, design, social media, advertising, web and digital development, SEO, storytelling, creative development, and audio/video production. ▪ Exceptional interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. ▪ Experience leading integrated marketing and communications strategies and trends. ▪ Understanding of higher education trends and audiences. ▪ Knowledge of brand development and standards, and of co-branding best practices. ▪ Knowledge of news reporting processes, ethical considerations, and best practices. ▪ Knowledge of the college enrollment process, including recruitment, admissions, financial aid, registration/enrollment, and student success. ▪ Demonstrated experience serving as the public spokesperson for a complex organization, representing institutional interests and communicating on sensitive and high-profile matters. ▪ Supervisory experience, including mentoring and providing professional development opportunities to staff. ▪ Knowledge of organizational planning, assessment, and budget oversight. ▪ Ability to function independently with minimum supervision. ▪ Knowledge of technology tools and systems, including Salesforce CRM, Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, Website Content Management systems, Project Management systems, data analysis and visualization software, and social media marketing and engagement platforms. Required Qualifications ▪ Minimum 10 years of progressively responsible experience in marketing, communications, brand management, or a related field. ▪ Minimum 4 years of management experience with direct supervision of team members. ▪ Bachelor’s degree or higher in marketing, communications, public relations, public administration, business administration, or a related field. ▪ Experience developing and monitoring budgets. ▪ Experience advising on chief executive communications. ▪ Experience in crisis communications. Preferred Qualifications ▪ Significant experience within higher education, the public sector, or similarly complex mission-driven organizations, with an understanding of shared governance, public accountability, and political context. ▪ Experience working in a marketing, communications, or creative agency environment. ▪ Experience managing relationships with multiple clients with diverse needs and subject matters. ▪ Master’s degree or higher in marketing, communications, public relations, public administration, business administration, or related field. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Communications and Marketing Management 4 Market Range – 16 ( Salary Schedules ) For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Position is contingent on a satisfactory background check ETSU Overview Nestled in the shadow of the Appalachian Mountains in Johnson City, Tennessee, East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is a thriving public research university and the flagship institution of the Appalachian Highlands. Since its founding in 1911, ETSU has remained steadfast in its mission to improve the quality of life for the people of the region and beyond through education, research, healthcare, and community engagement. Today, the University serves approximately 14,000 students through more than 160 undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs and is recognized for its commitment to student success, economic mobility, innovation, and public service. ETSU combines the opportunities of a comprehensive research university with a deeply personal and community-centered culture. The institution is ranked among the nation's leaders for student outcomes and affordability, with a strong reputation for helping graduates achieve social and economic mobility while graduating with comparatively low levels of debt. As an institution grounded in the values of hard work, service, and opportunity, ETSU is a place where students from all backgrounds are empowered to succeed and compete with the best. A defining strength of the University is its Academic Health Sciences Center, the largest public academic health sciences center in Tennessee. Through the Quillen College of Medicine, College of Nursing, College of Health Sciences, College of Public Health, the Gatton College of Pharmacy, as well as ETSU Health, the University prepares healthcare professionals, advances research, and expands access to care throughout the region. ETSU's integrated approach to education, research, and clinical service has established the institution as a national leader in rural health and community-focused healthcare. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer *PLEASE APPLY DIRECTLY AT THE LINK BELOW: https://wittkieffer.com/positions/a1wun0000024ufbmaq "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1200": {
      "title": "Integrated Clinical Psychologist",
      "description": "Category: Academic JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States The Department of Internal Medicine seeks an I ntegrated Clinical Psychologist to provide evidence-based behavioral health services within outpatient internal medicine clinics while also contributing to the academic mission of the Department and College of Medicine. This faculty position combines direct patient care with teaching, scholarship, mentorship, and service. The psychologist will work collaboratively as part of an interdisciplinary healthcare team to improve patient outcomes through integrated behavioral health services, while educating medical students, residents, fellows, and other healthcare professionals. The successful candidate will maintain an active clinical practice, participate in educational programs, develop scholarly activities, and contribute to departmental and institutional initiatives consistent with the expectations of a clinical-track Assistant Professor appointment. Key Responsibilities Include: Provide comprehensive psychological assessment, diagnosis, and evidence-based behavioral health interventions for adult patients within integrated Internal Medicine clinics. Collaborate with physicians and interdisciplinary healthcare teams to deliver integrated behavioral healthcare, including same-day consultations, treatment planning, and quality improvement initiatives. Maintain timely and accurate clinical documentation in the electronic health record and ensure compliance with applicable clinical standards. Teach and mentor medical students, residents, fellows, and other learners through clinical supervision, didactic instruction, and interdisciplinary educational activities. Engage in scholarly activities, including research, quality improvement, presentations, and publications, consistent with faculty expectations. Participate in departmental, college, and institutional committees, faculty meetings, and service activities that support the academic mission of the Department. Maintain professional licensure, pursue continuing professional development, and contribute to the advancement of integrated behavioral health programs within the Department. About the Quillen College of Medicine: East Tennessee State University’s Quillen College of Medicine is nationally recognized for its commitment to primary care education and service to rural and underserved populations. In the 2025 U.S. News & World Report rankings, Quillen College of Medicine was named a Tier 1 medical school for Primary Care and ranked #2 in the nation for Most Graduates Practicing in Medically Underserved Areas. If you are a dedicated Infectious Diseases/Critical Care Physician seeking to make a meaningful impact in a supportive, mission-driven academic environment, we encourage you to apply and become a valued member of the ETSU Quillen College of Medicine team. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of integrated behavioral healthcare and collaborative care models. Expertise in evidence-based psychological assessment and intervention. Ability to manage a diverse patient population with complex medical and behavioral health conditions. Strong teaching and mentoring skills. Ability to collaborate effectively across multiple disciplines. Strong clinical documentation and electronic health record proficiency. Excellent organizational, analytical, and problem-solving abilities. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and patient-centered care. Demonstrated commitment to professionalism, ethics, and lifelong learning. Demonstrated experience providing evidence-based psychological interventions with adult populations. Ability to work effectively within interdisciplinary healthcare teams. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Required Qualifications Ph.D in Clinical Psychology from an accredited institution. Completion of an APA-accredited internship Completion of Post-Doctoral Fellowship Licensed or license eligible as a Psychologist in the State of Tennessee (at time of hire) Compensation and Benefits Job Family– Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Based upon commensurate For information regarding benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Documents required to apply: Cover Letter, CV, and Doctoral Program Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1161": {
      "title": "Lecturer, DIGM/AI Generalist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Position Type: Full-Time Faculty Course Load: 4 courses per semester The Department of Digital Media seeks an innovative, forward-thinking Instructor of Digital Media with expertise in integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) into creative workflows and digital pipelines. The ideal candidate is a knowledgeable generalist capable of connecting modern AI tools and concepts across our four core concentrations: Game Design, Animation, Visualization, and VFX. Key Responsibilities Teaching: Teach a 4-course load per semester plus student mentoring, primarily focused on multiple sections of the foundational core Digital Media AI course. Instruction for our Digital Media AI courses; which will include: oversight of curriculum alignment across sections, updating course materials as industry tools evolve, and teaching multiple sections each semester. Course & Curriculum Coordination : Oversee and maintain the Digital Media AI curriculum, ensuring consistent learning outcomes, ethical AI framework integration, and up-to-date toolsets across all course sections. Student Mentorship: Guide students in leveraging emerging AI tech ethically, critically, and effectively within their artistic and technical pipelines. Departmental Engagement : Stay ahead of rapid advances in generative tools, procedural workflows, neural rendering, and interactive AI applications to ensure our program remains at the forefront of digital media education. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities AI Integration & Tools: Hands-on experience applying modern AI methodologies, workflows, and tools (e.g., visual generation, texture/asset synth, neural rendering, voice/audio synthesis, procedural AI tools, or script-assisted AI pipelines) within digital media creation. Broad Digital Media Generalist : Competency or practical familiarity across the four departmental concentrations: Game Design: Game engines (Unreal/Unity), interactive logic, emerging AI-driven gameplay assets or NPC logic. Animation : 2D/3D character animation pipelines, motion capture, AI-assisted rigging/animating workflows. Visualization: Architectural, scientific, or product visualization, 3D modeling, lighting, rendering pipelines. VFX: Compositing, rotoscoping, particle/simulation systems, AI-driven image processing and synthesis. Teaching & Communication: Strong communication skills and a passion for undergraduate education, curriculum development, and fostering ethical awareness around AI technology in creative disciplines. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a related technical/artistic field, or a Bachelor's degree paired with substantial professional industry experience and a strong portfolio demonstrating relevant expertise, will also be considered. Preferred Qualifications Master of Fine Arts (MFA) in Digital Media, Game Design, Animation, Computer Graphics, VFX, or a closely related field. Compensation & Benefits Salary: $75,000 For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Portfolio ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1199": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neonatologist- Assistant/Assoc Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Neonatologist – Division of Neonatology – East Tennessee State University – Mild 4-Season Climate, Situated in the Central Appalachian Highlands. The Department of Pediatrics at East Tennessee State University, Quillen College of Medicine, is seeking a full-time Neonatologist to join this division at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor and the rank will be commensurate with academic experience. This is a non-tenure track position. The position is a joint hire with Medical Education Assistance Corporation (MEAC). Responsibilities of the Neonatologist include providing clinical care for a 39-bed level III NICU with in-house nurse practitioners, outpatient high-risk neonatal follow-up, the teaching of medical students and pediatric residents, quality improvement, and academic pursuits. We have over 800 NICU admissions per year at Niswonger Children’s Hospital, with air and ground transport systems available. An active perinatology division for maternal evaluation and management is also present through the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. The review of applicants will continue until this position is filled. We offer a competitive salary and benefits package. Our region is located at the base of the Appalachian Mountains and offers excellent schools, a low cost of living, and a wealth of outdoor activities. Applicant may contact Dr. Jack Owens, Professor and Chief of Pediatric Neonatology, by email at owensjd@etsu.edu or call at 423-439-6222. *J-1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply Note: This position is contingent on external funding. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS At time of hire: MD/DO Completion of Neonatology fellowship. Board Certified in Pediatrics. BC/BE in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience For more information regarding benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copy of Transcripts Please note: Exempt positions are posted for a minimum of 14 calendar days. The closing date is subject to change without notice to the applicants. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution's focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
