    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1174": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, RHSC",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Nutrition and Integrated Health Sciences at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) invites applications for a 9-month clinical or tenure-track faculty appointment in the growing undergraduate Rehabilitative Health Sciences (RHSC-BS) program. The RHSC-BS program focuses on human function, disability, and rehabilitation through the perspectives of the health sciences, social sciences, psychology, and related disciplines. The program is distinctive in providing students interested in rehabilitative health professions with opportunities to develop skills in evidence-based practice, person-centered care, critical thinking, problem-solving, and interprofessional collaboration while working with diverse populations and across varied settings. The successful candidate will serve as a full member of the faculty and will participate in all relevant teaching, service, scholarly, and professional responsibilities associated with the appointment. The faculty member will teach a range of undergraduate courses within the RHSC-BS curriculum, which may include interprofessional rehabilitative practice, culture and disability, neurorehabilitation, ethics, clinical reasoning, disabilities across the lifespan, administrative principles, psychosocial aspects of disability, research, and technology in rehabilitation. The candidate may also contribute to undergraduate research and support an active student professional organization. The successful candidate will join a dynamic and growing department comprised of tenured, tenure-track, clinical-track, and support faculty and staff committed to interprofessional education and training. The Department is housed within the College of Health Sciences, which offers a broad range of undergraduate, graduate, and certificate programs, including Speech-Language Pathology, Audiology, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, Nutrition and Dietetics, Social Work, Exercise and Sports Science, Sports Nutrition, Prosthetics and Orthotics, and Allied Health Sciences. The College is part of ETSU’s Academic Health Sciences division, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, College of Public Health, and College of Nursing. ETSU is a comprehensive teaching and research university with an enrollment of approximately 14,500 students. Located in the scenic foothills of the Appalachian Mountains, Johnson City offers award-winning public schools, no state income tax, and a family-friendly environment with abundant opportunities for outdoor recreation and four distinct seasons. The rich history of the region is woven throughout its recreational opportunities, communities, and distinctive quality of life. The value of employment at ETSU extends beyond salary. Regular-benefit employees enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits, services, and programs, including paid time off and leave, paid holidays, health and life insurance, retirement benefits, and access to University facilities and services. ETSU is committed to ensuring that students, faculty, and staff are valued and supported in an environment characterized by openness, acceptance, and respect. Required Qualifications A terminal academic degree (e.g., PhD, EdD, ScD) in health and rehabilitative sciences or a related rehabilitation discipline, or a clinical doctorate (e.g., AuD, OTD, DPT, DHSc). Candidates who are ABD will be considered but must have completed the terminal degree by the time of hire. A minimum of two (2) years of professional work experience in a field of rehabilitation (e.g., OT, SLP, PT). Professional licensure in one of the following: Audiology, Communication Sciences, Dietetics, Occupational Therapy, Pharmaceutical Science, Physical Therapy, Speech-Language Pathology, Rehabilitative Counseling, or a closely related field. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate interprofessional rehabilitation education. Demonstrated commitment to teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with the mission of the University and the priorities of the College. Preferred Qualifications A terminal degree or clinical doctorate in Occupational Therapy, Speech-Language Pathology, or Physical Therapy. A proven record of teaching at the university level and research productivity. Potential for professional and scholarly productivity. Demonstrates success in a collaborative environment and/or working with diverse stakeholders. Compensation & Benefits Salary commensurate with experience For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions and additional details Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Cover letter, CV, and three references available upon request. Copies of transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1182": {
      "title": "Academic Infectious Diseases/Critical Care Physician",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The ETSU Department of Internal Medicine seeks a board-certified/board-eligible Infectious Disease/Critical Care Physician to join our growing academic division. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive inpatient and outpatient infectious disease care, participate in inpatient critical care services, educate medical students, residents, and fellows, and contribute to scholarly activity aligned with the academic mission of the institution. The position features a rotating schedule of one week (7 days) of inpatient Critical Care service, one week (7 days) off, and two weeks of combined inpatient and outpatient Infectious Disease practice per month. Key Responsibilities Include: Provide inpatient and outpatient Infectious Disease care, consultation, diagnosis, and management of complex infectious diseases across affiliated hospitals and ambulatory clinics. Serve as an attending physician on Critical Care services, providing management of critically ill patients, performing procedures consistent with training and hospital privileges, and participating in Infectious Disease and Critical Care call coverage. Collaborate with multidisciplinary healthcare teams to develop and implement evidence-based, patient-centered treatment plans and support antimicrobial stewardship, infection prevention, quality improvement, and patient safety initiatives. Teach, supervise, mentor, and evaluate medical students, residents, fellows, and other learners through clinical instruction, didactic lectures, conferences, simulation activities, and curriculum development. Engage in scholarly activity through clinical, translational, or outcomes research, including publications, presentations, grant development, and collaboration with interdisciplinary investigators. Participate in divisional, departmental, institutional, and professional committees; contribute to program development, strategic initiatives, community outreach, and continuing medical education. ID/CC faculty members benefit from the guidance of experienced academic leaders and access to robust institutional resources designed to support professional development and career growth. Due to the significant regional need for Infectious Disease services, faculty have the opportunity to make a meaningful and lasting impact on the health of the community. About the Quillen College of Medicine: East Tennessee State University’s Quillen College of Medicine is nationally recognized for its commitment to primary care education and service to rural and underserved populations. In the 2025 U.S. News & World Report rankings, Quillen College of Medicine was named a Tier 1 medical school for Primary Care and ranked #2 in the nation for Most Graduates Practicing in Medically Underserved Areas. If you are a dedicated Infectious Diseases/Critical Care Physician seeking to make a meaningful impact in a supportive, mission-driven academic environment, we encourage you to apply and become a valued member of the ETSU Quillen College of Medicine team. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of Infectious Disease and Critical Care Medicine principles, evidence-based practice, and regulatory requirements. Strong clinical judgment, diagnostic, and patient management skills in inpatient and outpatient settings. Effective teaching, mentoring, communication, and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in electronic health record documentation and clinical workflows. Ability to collaborate with multidisciplinary teams and provide high-quality, patient-centered care. Ability to engage in scholarly activity, quality improvement, and academic service while balancing clinical and educational responsibilities. Required Qualifications Medical Degree (MD, DO, or MBBS) from an accredited institution Successful completion of an Infectious Diseases/Critical Care fellowship from an ACGME-accredited program (at time of hire) Board Certified in Infectious Diseases/Critical Care or Board Eligible in Infectious Diseases/Critical Care (at time of interview) Preferred Qualifications Experience in medical education and academic medicine Interest in research, quality improvement, or program development Benefits and Compensation Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Based on Commensurate For information regarding benefits, please visit (https://www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Documents required to apply : Cover Letter , CV , and Medical School Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations "
    },
