    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/729": {
      "title": "Temporary Clerical - 968040",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Academic Proctor Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Availability to work on an as-needed basis during scheduled exam periods. Ability to work exam sessions typically scheduled during the following times: 9:00 AM - 11:00 AM 9:00 AM - 12:00 PM 1:00 PM - 3:00 PM 2:00 PM - 4:00 PM Ability to sit, stand, and walk throughout examination sessions. Ability to maintain a professional demeanor and exercise sound judgment in a testing environment. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent required; associate's degree or higher preferred. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive student and examination information with discretion. Strong attention to detail and the ability to follow written and verbal instructions accurately. Reliable, dependable, and punctual, with a demonstrated commitment to professionalism. Ability to remain attentive and focused throughout examination periods. Effective communication and interpersonal skills to interact professionally with students, faculty, and staff. Ability to enforce testing policies and procedures fairly and consistently. Basic computer skills and the ability to learn examination software and testing procedures as needed. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in an educational, testing, administrative, or customer service environment. Previous proctoring, tutoring, teaching, or student support experience. Experience working with college, university, or professional students. Familiarity with accommodating students who have approved testing accommodations. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1135": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neurologist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Pediatrics at East Tennessee State University (ETSU), Quillen College of Medicine, and Medical Education Assistance Corporation (MEAC) are seeking one full-time BC/BE Child Neurologist to join our large collegial group of pediatricians and pediatric specialty physicians in clinical care. You will be joining an established practice with two pediatric neurologists and three nurse practitioners. You will work in a new pediatric clinic and a beautiful pediatric hospital with a warm, child and family friendly environment, emerging to be one of the region’s largest tertiary referral centers. Established Pediatric Subspecialty Clinic representing 13 specialties in addition to a thriving outpatient patient base and pediatric hospital medicine program. 24-bed Pediatric Inpatient Unit staffed by 8 Pediatric Hospital Medicine physicians. 10-bed PICU Level III 44-bed NICU 24-hour EEG tech availability and remote EEG review capability Pediatric radiology, orthopedics, and genetics available Friendly college community that is a great place to raise a family near the majestic Appalachian Highlands Other Considerations for this Position: The position is at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Faculty rank commensurate with education and experience. Completion of child neurology fellowship is required at time of hire. While completion of epilepsy fellowship is not required, comfort with reading pediatric EEGs including neonatal, routine studies, ambulatory studies, and prolonged inpatient studies is required. This is a non-tenure, clinical track position. Academic responsibilities include teaching of medical students and pediatric residents as well as academic pursuits. Clinical responsibilities include providing clinical care at Niswonger Children’s Hospital, reading EEGs, and outpatient pediatric neurology clinic. Must be willing to assist in supervision of already trained pediatric neurology nurse practitioner. Competitive salary and benefit package, contingent on external funding. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach medical students and residents. Ability to perform routine and customary care of the inpatient and outpatient pediatric neurology patients. Required Qualifications: MD/DO Completion of Pediatric Neurology Fellowship at time of hire. Must be BC/BE in Pediatric Neurology at time of hire. Benefits and Compensation: Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Based on commensurate For information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) **This position is contingent upon outside funding. **J1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) Calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Required documents to attach: Cover Letter , CV , and Copy of Transcripts About the Region: Nestled in the foothills of the scenic Appalachian Highlands, Johnson City, TN combines big city amenities, small town charm, and world class outdoor recreation with living costs well below the national average. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1136": {
      "title": "Pediatric Endocrinologist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The Division of Pediatric Endocrinology at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is expanding to add a fourth pediatric endocrinologist to an enthusiastic team supported by advanced practitioners, diabetes educators, a pediatric endocrine nurse and dietician. Since opening in 2015, the clinic has thrived by investing in the community to provide excellent clinical care, teach the next generation of providers, engage in meaningful research and quality improvement, and advocate for our patients. The position is via a partnership with Ballad Health, the region’s health system encompassing 21 hospitals, of which Niswonger Children’s Hospital is the flagship pediatric institution for a catchment area of over 1 million people. We are the referral location for children requiring pediatric endocrine care in Northeast TN, Southwest VA, and portions of KY and WV. All pediatric endocrine care is focused at this one location (no satellite clinic travel). Inpatient endocrinology is a consult-only service supported by a strong intensivist and hospitalist team and pediatric residents. Established Pediatric Subspecialty Clinic representing 13 specialties in addition to a thriving outpatient patient base and pediatric hospital medicine program. 24-bed Pediatric Inpatient Unit staffed by 8 Pediatric Hospital Medicine physicians. 10-bed PICU Level III 44-bed NICU Friendly college community that is a great place to raise a family near the majestic Appalachian Highlands Other Considerations for this Position: The position is at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Faculty rank commiserate with education and experience. Completion of child endocrinology fellowship is required at time of hire. This is a non-tenure, clinical track position. Academic responsibilities include teaching of medical students and pediatric residents as well as academic pursuits. Competitive salary and benefit package, contingent on external funding. Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach medical students and residents. Ability to perform routine and customary care of the inpatient and outpatient pediatric endocrinology patients. Required Qualifications: MD/DO Completion of Pediatric Endocrinology Fellowship at time of hire. Must be BC/BE in Pediatric Endocrinology at time of hire. Benefits and Compensation: Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with prior experience. For information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) *J1 visa waiver candidates are encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) Calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Required documents to attach: Cover Letter , CV , and Copy of Transcripts About the Region: Nestled in the foothills of the scenic Appalachian Highlands, Johnson City, TN combines big city amenities, small town charm, and world class outdoor recreation with living costs well below the national average. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations "
