    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1156": {
      "title": "Clinical Academic Hematologist/Oncologist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Job Summary The ETSU Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Hematology and Oncology, invites board-certified or board-eligible Hematologists/Oncologists to join our established team at the Regional Cancer Center in Johnson City, Tennessee . Whether your passion lies in patient care, teaching, research, or academic leadership, your career will be supported and encouraged within our collaborative academic environment. This is a predominantly outpatient-focused position with a 4-day clinical schedule and one dedicated day for protected administrative time. Inpatient responsibilities are shared among faculty, with each physician covering one inpatient service week at a time. Key Responsibilities Include: Provide comprehensive outpatient hematology and oncology care Participate in shared inpatient hematology/oncology service coverage Teach and mentor medical students, residents, and fellows in both clinical and academic settings Deliver lectures, lead case discussions, and contribute to hands-on clinical education Engage in scholarly activity, quality improvement initiatives, and academic service. Participate in the fellowship recruitment and interview process. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to deliver patient-centered, evidence-based care Hematology/Oncology faculty members benefit from the guidance of experienced academic leaders and access to robust institutional resources designed to support professional development and career growth. Due to the significant regional need for hematology and oncology services, faculty have the opportunity to make a meaningful and lasting impact on the health of the community. Compensation aligns with AAMC salary recommendation benchmarks for academic hematology/oncology. About the Quillen College of Medicine: East Tennessee State University’s Quillen College of Medicine is nationally recognized for its commitment to primary care education and service to rural and underserved populations. In the 2025 U.S. News & World Report rankings, Quillen College of Medicine was named a Tier 1 medical school for Primary Care and ranked #2 in the nation for Most Graduates Practicing in Medically Underserved Areas . If you are a dedicated Hematologist/Oncologist seeking to make a meaningful impact in a supportive, mission-driven academic environment, we encourage you to apply and become a valued member of the ETSU Quillen College of Medicine team. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Comprehensive knowledge of hematology and oncology clinical practice and evidence-based care Ability to manage complex oncologic and hematologic conditions in both outpatient and inpatient settings Strong teaching and mentoring skills for medical trainees Excellent interpersonal and communication skills for multidisciplinary collaboration Proficiency in electronic health record documentation and clinical workflows Commitment to professionalism, ethical practice, and patient-centered care Ability to balance clinical, educational, and scholarly responsibilities Required Qualifications Medical Degree (MD, DO, or MBBS) from an accredited institution Successful completion of a Hematology/Oncology fellowship from an ACGME-accredited program (at time of hire) Board Certified in Hematology/Oncology or Board Eligible in Hematology/Oncology (at time of interview) Preferred Qualifications Experience in medical education and academic medicine Interest in research, quality improvement, or program development Benefits and Compensation Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Based on commensurate For information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Documents required to apply: Cover Letter , CV and Medical School Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1130": {
      "title": "Newborn Hospitalist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Pediatric Newborn Hospitalist – Division of Pediatric Hospital Medicine – East Tennessee State University- Mild 4-Season Climate, Situated in the Central Appalachian Highlands. The Department of Pediatrics at East Tennessee State University (ETSU), Quillen College of Medicine, and Medical Education Assistance Corporation (MEAC), in conjunction with Ballad Health seeks a qualified Newborn Pediatric Hospitalist to join a dynamic team of hospitalists. Experience should include: Demonstrated skill in newborn medicine Demonstrated skill in Neonatal Resuscitation and stabilization for transport Experience in medical education Experience in quality improvement is a plus Willingness to perform circumcisions This position will be an ETSU non-tenure, clinical track faculty appointment (contingent on external funding). Faculty rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. The successful candidate will receive a full benefits package through ETSU. Responsibilities include providing nursery services and delivery attendance at multiple Ballad Health level 1 newborn nurseries in the region, including but not limited to Franklin Woods Community Hospital, Indian Path Community Hospital, and Niswonger Children’s Hospital, the region’s primary pediatric inpatient site. Clinical coverage at Niswonger Children’s Hospital would also include potential daytime rounding on lower acuity level III NICU coverage. There is an opportunity for involvement with quality improvement, patient safety, and medical student and resident education. The review of applicants will continue until this position is filled. We offer a competitive salary and benefits package. Our region is located at the base of the Appalachian Mountains and offers excellent schools, a low cost of living, and a wealth of outdoor activities. Required Qualifications At time of hire: MD/DO BC/BE in pediatrics at time of hire Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Salary – Based on commensurate For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar day. This is subject to change without notice to the applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attached the following documents : Cover Letter , CV and Copy of Transcripts ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, and recent strategic initiatives that prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations . "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1154": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Mechatronics Engineering, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Engineering, Engineering Technology and Surveying at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is seeking to hire a tenure track assistant/associate professor in Mechatronics Engineering starting August 15, 2027. This is a 9-month faculty position. The successful candidate will primarily teach in the undergraduate mechatronics engineering program. Responsibilities include teaching a variety of undergraduate courses and laboratories in areas such robotics, electromechanical systems, robotic systems integration, vision systems, autonomous systems, collaborative robotics, sensors and actuators, network security systems, and advanced data acquisition systems and other mechatronics courses. The candidate is also expected to maintain an active externally funded research portfolio and supervise graduate students. Additionally, the role also involves supporting ABET accreditation activities and the senior design project in the mechatronics program. Other duties include directing student projects, participating in student recruitment events, engaging in departmental and institutional service activities, and perform other tasks/duties assigned by the department chair. The Department of Engineering, Engineering Technology, Interior Architecture and Surveying is housed within the College of Arts and Sciences in the newly formed School of Sciences, Engineering and Math. The department is a multidisciplinary department with 19 faculty and support staff. The department offers one ABET-accredited General Engineering program, a new Mechatronics Engineering program, and four ABET-accredited Engineering Technology programs in Biomedical, Construction, Electronics, and Manufacturing. The department also offers a CIDA-accredited Interior Architecture and an ABET-accredited Surveying and Mapping program. The department has an MS in Engineering Technology program with two concentrations including Robotics, Automation, and Instrumentation Systems Concentration. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to inspire and motivate students using hands-on, applied, and experiential learning. Knowledge of student-centered and innovative instructional strategies including online teaching experience. Ability to effectively and respectfully work, communicate, and collaborate in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings. A strong commitment to undergraduate engineering education. Required Qualifications The candidate must have a Ph.D. in Mechatronics Engineering or one of the closely related engineering areas: Mechanical, Industrial, Electrical, Robotics, by the hire date. OR M.S. in Mechatronics Engineering or in one of the above listed areas. The M.S. candidate will have a minimum of 10 years of teaching or industrial experience in areas related to the job description. Successful record of research and applied scholarly activities in the above listed areas. Laboratory instruction and facility management experience, including but not limited to safety, supervision, and procurement. Demonstrated experience and commitment to collaboratively work in multidisciplinary settings. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience and curriculum design in engineering areas. Candidates who have proven track records of relevant industry and practical experiences. A robust track record of publication and extramurally funded research. Experience with ABET accreditation processes. Compensation & Benefits Salary: $90,000 For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Initial review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests A list of three references with contact information For additional information, please contact Dr. Paul Sims, Search Committee Chair, at simsj@etsu.edu . ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1162": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Construction Engineering, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Engineering, Engineering Technology and Surveying at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is seeking to hire a tenure track assistant professor in Construction Engineering or a closely related field starting August 15, 2027. This is a 9-month faculty position. The successful candidate will primarily teach in the undergraduate construction engineering technology (CET) program. Responsibilities include teaching a variety of undergraduate courses and laboratories in areas such as statics, engineering mechanics, construction fundamentals, construction materials, structural/steel design, thermal and fluid design and other construction courses. The candidate is also expected to maintain an active externally funded research portfolio and supervise graduate students. Additionally, the role also involves supporting ABET accreditation activities and the senior design project in the CET program. Other duties include directing student projects, participating in student recruitment events, engaging in departmental and institutional service activities, and perform other tasks/duties assigned by the department chair. The Department of Engineering, Engineering Technology, Interior Architecture and Surveying is housed within the College of Arts and Sciences in the newly formed School of Sciences, Engineering and Math. The department is a multidisciplinary department with 19 faculty and support staff. The department offers one ABET-accredited General Engineering program, a new Mechatronics Engineering program, and four ABET-accredited Engineering Technology programs in Biomedical, Construction, Electronic, and Manufacturing. The department also offers a CIDA-accredited Interior Architecture and an ABET-accredited Surveying and Mapping program. The department has an MS in Engineering Technology program with two concentrations including Digital Construction and Data Analytics. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to inspire and motivate students using hands-on, applied, and experiential learning. Knowledge of student-centered and innovative instructional strategies including online teaching experience. Ability to effectively and respectfully work, communicate, and collaborate in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings. A strong commitment to undergraduate engineering education. Required Qualifications The candidate must have a Ph.D. in Construction or Civil Engineering (or a closely related field) by the hire date. Successful record of research and applied scholarly activities. Experiences in laboratory and hands-on instruction. Demonstrated experience and commitment to collaboratively work in multidisciplinary settings. Preferred Qualifications Minimum of two years of experience in the construction industry. A strong record of scholarly publications and externally funded research. Experience with ABET accreditation processes. Professional Engineering (P.E.) licensure, or the ability to obtain licensure in the State of Tennessee. Compensation & Benefits Salary: $90,000.00 For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Initial review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests A list of three references with contact information For additional information, please contact Dean Isham, Search Committee Chair, at ishamd@etsu.edu . ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
