    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1146": {
      "title": "PRN Nurse Practitioner Floater, Nursing Office of Practice",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU College of Nursing, Office of Practice invites applications for a PRN Family Nurse Practitioner Floater to support multiple nursing clinics. The Nurse Practitioner (NP) provides advanced primary care services in accordance with the Tennessee Nurse Practice Act. This role is responsible for assessing, diagnosing, and managing both acute and chronic health conditions across the lifespan. The Nurse Practitioner maintains accurate and timely documentation of all patient encounters and clinical services provided. The Nurse Practitioner provides supervision and guidance to assigned clinical and support staff, fostering a collaborative and efficient care environment. Participation in quality assurance and continuous improvement activities is an essential part of the role, ensuring adherence to best practices and regulatory standards. A strong commitment to health equity and the needs of vulnerable and underserved populations is central to this position, reflecting the clinic’s mission and values. Work Location and Travel: This is a floating position that provides coverage at multiple clinic locations as needed. Employees report directly to their assigned clinic each workday. Travel reimbursement is provided only for travel to Hancock County. Position Status: This is a temporary position with the potential to become permanent based on organizational needs, funding, and employee performance. Permanent employment is not guaranteed. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and skill in assessment, diagnoses, and treatment of common acute and chronic health conditions. Knowledge of recognized standards of care. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Ability to organize and set priorities. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) with preparation in advanced practice nursing (PMHNP, FNP, ANP, PNP or other specialty as required for position.) Current unencumbered license as Registered Nurse in Tennessee or compact state. National certification in appropriate area. Certificate of fitness to prescribe. Experience as specified for each position. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of experience in advanced practice nursing (FNP, ANP, PNP or other specialty as required for position.) Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by the employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job across various settings in the classroom, simulation, clinical, and/or community. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, climb, reach, and balance. The employee may occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, and/or move more than 100 pounds. The employee must be able to perceive and respond to sounds and alarms; communicate effectively with others; and have a sufficient vision regarding near, distance, color, peripheral, and depth perception as well as the ability to observe and monitor situations in full and dimmed light. The employee may stand, walk, and/or sit in various settings for up to 12 hours at a time in addition to the preparation and closure of a clinical shift. Rapid mobility may also be required on occasion. Physical expectations of an assigned clinical facility may vary and be subject to change. Stress levels may be high due to frequently dealing with numerous students, patients, family members, and other healthcare providers. This position demands concentration and the ability to work in emotionally-charged situations. Compensation & Benefits Hourly rate based upon education and experience. Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents required to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume Copy of current unencumbered RN licensure from TN or multi-state. Copy of National Board Certification. Copy of Certificate of fitness to prescribe. An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. College of Nursing Overview The College of Nursing is part of the University’s Academic Health Sciences Center, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is the largest in the State of Tennessee, offering multiple tracks for students enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs. The nurse-led clinics under the College of Nursing feature four Federally Qualified Health Centers and two Student Health Clinics. The largest Community Health Center in Johnson City provides primary care, behavioral health care, pediatrics, and women's health with an on-site Dental Clinic, Radiology Department, Lab, and Charitable Pharmacy. Area unhoused individuals receive a continuum of services at the Downtown Day Center. Two school-based clinics in Hancock County provide care for students, staff, and the surrounding community. ETSU students and staff are served by the University Health Center on campus, while the nurse clinic at University School serves that population. The College of Nursing Community Health Centers have received federal funding for more than 30 years, accepting all patients regardless of their ability to pay. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1147": {
      "title": "PRN Women's Health Nurse Practitioner, Nursing Office of Practice",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States The ETSU College of Nursing, Office of Practice invites applications for a PRN Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner Floater to support multiple nursing clinics. The Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner (WHNP) provides advanced primary and women's healthcare services in accordance with the Tennessee Nurse Practice Act. This role is responsible for assessing, diagnosing, and managing acute and chronic health conditions, while delivering comprehensive gynecologic, reproductive, and low-risk prenatal care across the lifespan. The WHNP maintains accurate and timely documentation of all patient encounters and clinical services provided. The Nurse Practitioner provides supervision and guidance to assigned clinical and support staff, fostering a collaborative and efficient care environment. Participation in quality assurance and continuous improvement activities is an essential part of the role, ensuring adherence to best practices and regulatory standards. A strong commitment to health equity and the needs of vulnerable and underserved populations is central to this position, reflecting the clinic's mission and values. Work Location and Travel: This is a floating position that provides coverage at multiple clinic locations as needed. Employees report directly to their assigned clinic each workday. Travel reimbursement is provided only for travel to Hancock County. Position Status: This is a temporary position with the potential to become permanent based on organizational needs, funding, and employee performance. Permanent employment is not guaranteed. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficiency in providing comprehensive well-woman care, including annual gynecologic examinations, cervical cancer screening (PAP tests), clinical breast examinations, contraceptive counseling, and ordering appropriate preventive screenings, including mammography. Knowledge and skill in assessment, diagnoses, and treatment of common acute and chronic health conditions. Knowledge of recognized standards of care. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Ability to organize and set priorities. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) or Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) with preparation in women’s health. Current unencumbered license as Registered Nurse in Tennessee or compact state. National certification in appropriate area. Certificate of fitness to prescribe. Experience as specified for each position. Current NEXPLANON REMS Certification (Insertion and Removal), or ability to obtain certification upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of experience in advanced practice nursing (FNP, ANP, PNP or other specialty as required for position.) Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by the employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job across various settings in the classroom, simulation, clinical, and/or community. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, climb, reach, and balance. The employee may occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, and/or move more than 100 pounds. The employee must be able to perceive and respond to sounds and alarms; communicate effectively with others; and have a sufficient vision regarding near, distance, color, peripheral, and depth perception as well as the ability to observe and monitor situations in full and dimmed light. The employee may stand, walk, and/or sit in various settings for up to 12 hours at a time in addition to the preparation and closure of a clinical shift. Rapid mobility may also be required on occasion. Physical expectations of an assigned clinical facility may vary and be subject to change. Stress levels may be high due to frequently dealing with numerous students, patients, family members, and other healthcare providers. This position demands concentration and the ability to work in emotionally-charged situations. Compensation & Benefits Hourly rate based upon education and experience. Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents required to apply: Cover Letter Current CV/Resume Copy of current unencumbered RN licensure from TN or multi-state. Copy of National Board Certification. Copy of Certificate of fitness to prescribe. Copy of current NEXPLANON REMS certification. An official transcript will be required upon hire. Copies and/or unofficial transcripts will be acceptable for application purposes only. Position is contingent upon available funding. College of Nursing Overview The College of Nursing is part of the University’s Academic Health Sciences Center, which also includes the James H. Quillen College of Medicine, the Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, the College of Public Health, and the College of Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is the largest in the State of Tennessee, offering multiple tracks for students enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs. The nurse-led clinics under the College of Nursing feature four Federally Qualified Health Centers and two Student Health Clinics. The largest Community Health Center in Johnson City provides primary care, behavioral health care, pediatrics, and women's health with an on-site Dental Clinic, Radiology Department, Lab, and Charitable Pharmacy. Area unhoused individuals receive a continuum of services at the Downtown Day Center. Two school-based clinics in Hancock County provide care for students, staff, and the surrounding community. ETSU students and staff are served by the University Health Center on campus, while the nurse clinic at University School serves that population. The College of Nursing Community Health Centers have received federal funding for more than 30 years, accepting all patients regardless of their ability to pay. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1084": {
      "title": "Nurse Supervisor",
      "description": "Category: Medical Practice JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary ETSU Department of Internal Medicine seeks an experienced and motivated Nursing Supervisor to lead the daily clinical operations of our Infectious Diseases Clinic. This is a leadership opportunity for a registered nurse (RN) who is passionate about delivering exceptional patient care while supporting a collaborative, multidisciplinary healthcare team. As the Nursing Supervisor, you will work closely with the Executive Director to oversee the day-to-day functions of the clinic, including coordinating provider schedules, managing laboratory ordering and scheduling, providing clinical triage, monitoring patient flow, administering vaccines, and coordinating prior authorizations. You will play a key role in ensuring the clinic operates efficiently by maintaining medical supplies and medications, overseeing examination and procedure room readiness, ensuring emergency equipment is properly stocked, and coordinating the maintenance of clinical equipment. In this leadership position, you will supervise and mentor nursing staff, develop and implement clinical policies and procedures, and foster a culture of teamwork, accountability, and continuous improvement. You will also provide education and coaching to staff while ensuring compliance with HIPAA and other regulatory standards to maintain the highest level of patient care and confidentiality. If you are a strong clinical leader with excellent organizational and communication skills who thrives in a fast-paced academic healthcare environment, we encourage you to apply and join our mission of providing outstanding care to patients with infectious diseases while supporting education, research, and innovation. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of state institution procedure. Knowledge of the current health sciences and nursing procedures as practiced in generalist medical office setting. Knowledge of health care insurance, including private insurance, Medicare, and TennCare. Knowledge of organizational management and administration. Knowledge of various state, federal, and agency regulations. Knowledge of various patient referral/educational resources. Knowledge of lCD and CPT coding. Knowledge of medical terminology. Ability to fulfill all the expectations of the RN Scope of Practice. Ability to communicate professionally and effectively within a diverse clinical setting. Ability to analyze, revise, and develop nursing policies and procedures. Ability to effectively supervise staff. Ability to coordinate, analyze, and synthesize data. Ability to present training in a clear, concise manner and evaluate training outcomes. Ability to exercise sound judgement in evaluating situations and making decisions. Ability to handle confidential information appropriately, maintain compliance with HIPAA. Ability to meet deadlines and track/report information accurately. Ability to analyze workflow and make adjustments for optimum efficiency. Ability to utilize electronic health records for daily operations and to train others. Ability to standard office software, programs, and equipment. Ability to communicate effectively. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus three (3) years of current RN experience OR Associate degree in Nursing plus five (5) to seven (7) years of progressively responsible RN experience Must possess current Tennessee license as a Registered Nurse Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Medical Nurse 2 Salary MR 8 ($60,017.32 - $65,268.83) For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Health Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter , Resume and Copy of RN License Important Notes Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This position requires on-site work University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1095": {
      "title": "Community Health Navigator (HIV/STI Focus)",
      "description": "Category: Social Service JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary ETSU Infectious Diseases is seeking a compassionate and motivated Community Health Navigator (HIV/STI Focus) to join our team serving the Johnson City and Kingsport communities. In this vital role, you will help individuals access HIV/STI prevention and care services by providing intensive care coordination, patient navigation, and community outreach. Working closely with patients, providers, and community partners, you will support HIV/STI testing, harm reduction initiatives, PrEP navigation, and linkage to HIV/STI care, ensuring patients receive the resources and ongoing support needed to achieve positive health outcomes. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who is passionate about reducing barriers to care, promoting sexual health, and making a meaningful impact in the lives of underserved populations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of culturally competent, patient-centered care with an understanding of health disparities and barriers to healthcare access. Experience providing HIV/STI prevention education, including PrEP/PEP counseling, risk assessments, readiness screening, and risk-reduction coaching. Ability to provide HIV/STI testing and client-centered pre- and post-test counseling. Knowledge of HIV prevention and treatment resources, with the ability to connect clients to medical care, supportive services, and community resources. Experience assisting patients with insurance navigation, patient assistance programs (PAP), PrEP Assistance Program (PrEP-AP), AIDS Drug Assistance Program (ADAP), and other financial assistance resources. Ability to coordinate follow-up care, support medication adherence, schedule appointments, and assist with transportation when needed. Strong collaboration and communication skills with healthcare providers, care teams, and community partners to support high-quality HIV prevention and care services. Ability to maintain accurate documentation, ensure data integrity, and protect patient confidentiality in accordance with HIPAA and organizational policies. Experience developing and participating in community outreach, health fairs, educational events, and targeted engagement strategies to reach underserved and high-risk populations. Ability to provide inclusive sexual health education and build partnerships with organizations serving LGBTQ+, BIPOC, and other priority communities. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in public health, social services, or a related field and one to two (1–2) years of case management experience, or an equivalent combination of education and directly related experience. Preferred Qualifications Master of Social Work Degree Experience in HIV/STI counseling, prevention, and support services Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Social Services Professional 2 Salary MR 7 – ($53,112.67) For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Health Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter and Resume Important Notes Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This position requires on-site work. University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
