      "title": "Custodian, Housing",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Under close supervision, performs routine custodial and grounds maintenance duties to ensure a clean, safe, and well-maintained environment. Responsibilities include cleaning and maintaining public areas of academic and administrative buildings, medical facilities, residence halls, and apartments; assisting with the upkeep of assigned grounds; and completing all assigned cleaning tasks. Employees must be able to work any shift, and overtime may be required as needed. Performs duties under general supervision and determines the methods and sequence for completing assigned work. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of custodial cleaning methods, equipment, and chemicals. Knowledge of basic safety and sanitation practices. Skill in cleaning and maintaining facilities. Skill in following instructions and managing assigned tasks. Ability to perform physical work, including lifting, bending, and standing for extended periods. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to work any shift and overtime as required. Ability to maintain a clean, safe, and orderly environment. Required Qualifications Successful completion of the eighth grade. Knowledge of basic custodial cleaning methods, materials, and equipment. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services Buildings and Grounds Assistant 1 Market Range - 2 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit Employee Benefits Application Instructions and additional details Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate 