    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/683": {
      "title": "Clery Coordinator & Assistant Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Category: Audit & Compliance JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary This position serves as the University's Clery Coordinator, with primary responsibility for coordinating and overseeing institutional compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and its implementing regulations. The position manages Clery crime data collection and reconciliation, Clery geography determinations, coordination with campus and local law enforcement, preparation of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, issuance of required Clery notices, policy review, and training of Campus Security Authorities. In a secondary capacity, the position supports the Office of University Compliance by assisting with formal compliance investigations and related regulatory responsibilities, as assigned. These duties are subordinate to the position's primary Clery Act coordination function. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Working knowledge of the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and its implementing regulations. Knowledge of federal and state higher education compliance frameworks, including campus safety, civil rights, and institutional reporting obligations. Knowledge of higher education governance structures, institutional policies, and law enforcement coordination. Knowledge of investigative standards, due process principles, and confidentiality requirements applicable to compliance investigations. Ability to interpret and apply complex regulatory requirements to varied and fact-specific situations. Ability to analyze, reconcile, and validate institutional data from multiple sources for regulatory reporting purposes. Strong written communication skills, including the ability to draft formal reports, regulatory disclosures, and training materials. Strong interpersonal skills, including the ability to communicate with law enforcement, administrators, faculty, and staff regarding sensitive compliance matters. Ability to manage competing deadlines and regulatory timelines with minimal supervision. Ability to monitor, interpret, and apply evolving federal guidance, regulatory updates, and enforcement trends that impact Clery Act compliance and related civil rights obligations. Ability to exercise independent judgment in applying institutional policy and regulatory standards and to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Ability to assess institutional risk and escalate issues appropriately. Ability to work independently under general direction and to develop processes or procedures in response to changing regulatory requirements. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or Associate's Degree/Two years of College +Two (2) years of related work experience or four (4) years of related work experience Experience with regulatory compliance, investigations, and/or higher education compliance. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree, Juris Doctor (JD), and/or PhD. Clery Act compliance experience Law enforcement experience Title IX/civil rights compliance experience Higher education experience Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Audit/Compliance Officer 2 Market Range - 9 Salary Schedules For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter, Resume, and three (3) references University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/870": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, English",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Department of Literature and Language at East Tennessee State University seeks qualified instructors to fill part-time positions teaching English courses. Located in the Appalachian Highlands of Northeast Tennessee between the Great Smoky Mountains and the Blue Ridge Mountains, East Tennessee State University is a state-assisted and Carnegie-classified Doctoral Research Intensive University of more than 15,000 students. The Department of Literature and Language is a large, vibrant, and diverse department made up of English, World Languages, Film and Media Studies, Creative Writing, and other related disciplines. The successful candidates’ primary duties will be to teach English courses. Adjunct faculty primarily teach 1000- and 2000-level courses in person and/or online. These are temporary, adjunct positions, filled on a semester-by-semester basis with some opportunity for renewal. Adjunct faculty positions do not include benefits. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will be qualified to teach courses in English. Experience teaching English courses in a post-secondary setting. Required Qualifications The ideal candidate will have a Master's degree in English or a closely-related field. Candidates with at least 18 graduate credit hours in a relevant field will also be considered. Equivalent combinations of education and directly related professional experience may also be considered. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
