    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/429": {
      "title": "Academic -OB/GYN Hospitalist",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary East Tennessee State University’s (ETSU) The Quillen College of Medicine, Department of OB/GYN is accepting applications for full-time and/or part-time Hospitalist/Assistant Professor at the Johnson City Medical Center/Niswonger Children’s Hospital. The hospitalist will serve as the attending physician for hospital coverage for the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. This provider will provide coverage for the ETSU OB/GYN hospital service and provide supervision and education of resident physicians and medical students from ETSU. The Physician is responsible for coverage of labor and delivery, emergency department, inpatient consultations, and OB/GYN inpatient admissions and OB/GYN patient transfers. They will be in attendance for all resident-performed procedures during their assigned shifts. Supervision of care of triage patients will be expected to allow for compensation for these visits. The expected time commitment for a Full-Time Faculty will average two (2) twenty-four-hour shifts per week (eight shifts per month), but the number and timing are flexible. These shifts will occur during both weekday and weekend days and be assigned in conjunction with the other OB/GYN hospitalists and general OB/GYN physicians in the call rotation. Holidays are included on a rotating basis with the other faculty sharing calls. Completion of corresponding medical records and billing worksheets is required. Evaluations of students and resident physicians will be performed on an ongoing basis. Clinical education in the form of didactic lectures, informal discussions, and precepting is expected. Clinical research and performance improvement projects, in conjunction with residents and students, will be expected. Participation in the hospital department and hospital committees is encouraged. This position will report to the Chair of the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. The position is based on an annual renewal contract assuming deliverables are achieved. Our OB/GYN service coverage is focused at Niswonger Children’s, where we deliver approximately 1400 patients, both patients from our ETSU clinics as well as referred patients from other facilities in NE Tennessee and SW Virginia. These referrals are for our OB/GYN expertise as well as our Neonatology services and NICU. Maternal Fetal Medicine consultation services are available 24/7. A portion of this position may be grant-funded. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of general academic policies and curriculum issues Knowledge of Tennessee Board of Regents policies. Knowledge of accreditation policies where appropriate. Ability to engage in constructive problem-solving and to make sound decisions Ability to communicate effectively with faculty and staff within the department, college, university, and diverse campus and community constituencies. Ability to work collaboratively with the leadership of other academic and administrative units to develop appropriate policies and/or programs. Ability to promote student success and faculty excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Required Qualifications MD or DO degree, BC or BE in OB/GYN at time of hire. Preferred Qualifications Previous OB/GYN experience preferred Demonstrated experience /interest in women’s health Physical Demands Up to 50 lbs. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 4 Compensation is competitive with the Market and based on education and experience. For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/500": {
      "title": "Center for Academic Achievement - Temporary Pool (965090)",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Learning Services is currently hiring exceptional students to fill open positions as academic coaches, supplemental instruction (SI) leaders, and tutors. Each role provides a unique form of academic support to ETSU students. Academic Coaches will… Conduct weekly meetings with approximately 20 assigned students to promote their academic success Help students develop the skills needed to achieve academic goals by cultivating good study habits (time management, organization, motivation, note taking, effective study strategies, active reading and listening, test preparation, and more) Maintain files for each assigned student to help track progress and modify strategies as needed Complete brief session summary reports for each student meeting Build rapport and open communication channels with assigned students Supplemental Instruction leaders will… Attend all class meetings of the selected course, taking notes and following along with assigned readings Plan and conduct four 1-hour study and review sessions every week (2 on-ground and 2 on Zoom) Submit weekly SI session plans via D2L Participate in mandatory training held the week before classes begin and throughout the semester Tutors will… Attend all scheduled tutoring shifts Conduct one-on-one and occasional group sessions with ETSU students Review coursework, topics, and assignments with students to provide support with a variety of academic tasks Provide advice and strategies about skills to improve academic performance Participate in mandatory training held the week before classes begin and throughout the semester. PLEASE SEE APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS BEFORE APPLYING FOR THE POSITION. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to support and promote student success through effective academic guidance and encouragement. Proven reliability and strong sense of responsibility in meeting commitments and maintaining professional standards. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal, to effectively engage with diverse student populations and campus partners. Strong patience, empathy, and understanding when working with at-risk or struggling students. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive student information with discretion and professionalism. Required Qualifications Must be a current ETSU student with sophomore standing or higher Must maintain an overall GPA of 3.0 or higher Must have earned a grade of B+ or better in the course(s) you wish to support Must have a recommendation from a faculty member or advisor (For Academic Coaches) Must have a flexible schedule to accommodate a variety of weekly meeting times with students Preferred Qualifications Ability and desire to assist in multiple courses or subject areas. Compensation $10 – $15 per hour Application Instructions Non-Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Please include the following information on you applicantion / resume: Three (3) references, with at least one being a professor or academic advisor ETSU eNumber Which position you are interested in: tutor, academic coach, or SI leader? If applying for tutoring or SI, which courses you are able to support? University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
