    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/331": {
      "title": "Air Condition/Heating Mechanic 3",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Employees in this classification work under general supervision and are responsible for maintaining industrial PC (IN PC) equipment, control systems, and refrigeration systems. Duties include troubleshooting, repairing, calibrating, and replacing pneumatic controls, electric controls, and DOC control systems. Employees also perform routine and preventive maintenance, repair or replace compressors and related components, and use specialized test equipment, power tools, precision measuring instruments, plumbing tools, and standard hand tools. Additional responsibilities include ordering parts and supplies, operating service trucks, and maintaining boiler control systems. Must be able to work any shift or schedule. Overtime will be required as necessary. Facilities employees may be required to report at their regularly scheduled times during emergency closures or during inclement weather to perform essential functions, including snow removal duties. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of central chilled water systems and associated distribution equipment (preferred) Knowledge of steam distribution systems (preferred) Knowledge of Hydronic HVAC systems Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED required Must possess an EPA Universal Refrigerant Certification Valid Driver's License Two years of relevant experience or equivalent training Preferred Qualifications Three (3) years of HVAC/Mechanical Systems or relevant experience Experience in working with variable volume air conditioning systems Electrician License and controls experience Physical Demands Ability to climb ladders, steps, and scaffolds Ability to crawl, bend, twist, squat, and kneel Ability to lift and pull 50 lbs. on a repetitive basis Compensation & Benefits Job Family - Facilities Services Trades Specialist 3 Market Range - 6 ( Salary Schedules ) For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Non-exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/289": {
      "title": "Data Integrity Coordinator (Temporary)",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Center for Community Outreach and Applied Research is accepting applications for a Temporary Data Integrity Coordinator. The Center for Community Outreach oversees and carries out service grants for various State or Local Workforce Board organizations. Each grant is specific to the work being performed; therefore, this clerical/support position will serve a particular grant within the department where there is a need. Duties may include but are not limited to communicating with grant participants, serving as data input or compiler, communicating with internal employees within the specific grant or with external grant partners to ensure 100% consistency with data input, communicating with community vendors to provide support services to individuals, document program compliance for grant recipients, or operating client transportation payment systems by working with the Center’s QuickBooks data entry system. Positions will be home-based across TN and may require limited travel. The applicant must reside inside the state of Tennessee to be considered. This temporary position has the potential to transition into a full-time regular position based on performance, funding availability, and departmental needs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : High proficiency in Microsoft Excel. Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to work in a detail-oriented environment. Computer and technology skills. Required Qualifications High School Diploma or GED. Preferred Qualifications Some college. Knowledge of QuickBooks Knowledge of the Tennessee Department of Human Services, American Job Center System, or other government programs. Application Instructions Non-Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. University Overview East Tennessee Stat