    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1407": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator, Temporary",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Project Coordinator will provide coordination and administrative support for a federally funded OSHA program. This is a part-time position (20 hours per week) responsible for supporting the Principal Investigator, project faculty, trainers, and other project personnel in the planning, coordination, implementation, and documentation of grant activities. Responsibilities include trainee recruiting, supporting program logistics, maintaining records, assisting with reporting requirements, and helping to ensure compliance with OSHA timelines. The position will also coordinate scheduling, act as a liaison for facility/rental arrangements, and provide administrative support for training activities. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of occupational safety and health training programs. Familiarity with OSHA regulations, occupational safety and health training requirements, or federally funded training programs. Required Qualifications Undergraduate degree: BS or BA Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating occupational safety and health training programs. Experience recruiting trainees or participants from industrial settings. Experience working directly with industrial companies, employers, or workforce organizations. Familiarity with OSHA regulations, occupational safety and health training requirements, or federally funded training programs. Experience with grant administration, reporting, compliance documentation, or program evaluation. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
