    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1378": {
      "title": "Temporary Technical - Simulation Technician",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary (This is a temporary position) The Department of Academic Affairs in the College of Medicine is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Simulation Technician for a Temporary Hourly position to support the operations of the Simulation Laboratory. This position works closely with the Manager of Simulation and a full-time technician to ensure the effective delivery of simulation-based education and skills training. Responsibilities include assisting with the preparation, maintenance, and operation of simulation equipment and audiovisual systems to support educational activities for students, faculty, and staff. This position is contingent upon sufficient funding. Key Responsibilities Perform technical duties of a physical or biological nature to support research activities. Assist with data collection, interpretation, evaluation, and documentation for lab projects. Operate and set up laboratory or research equipment for experiments. Collect, tabulate, and calculate data using various electronic devices. Maintain computer databases of research and protocol records. Order, replace, and maintain laboratory supplies. Conduct minor repairs on research equipment as needed. Perform general laboratory maintenance and cleanup. Train and supervise new research personnel. Carry out additional duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of research Knowledge of business English and arithmetic. Ability to perform basic informational research projects. Ability to gather, compile, and analyze data. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues and the public. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Excel. Required Qualifications Experience as an RN, LPN, Respiratory Therapist, EMT, or paramedic Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a health-related field OR Bachelor's degree plus two years of experience in a health care setting Medical simulation experience Compensation Salary: $45 per hour (5 hours per week) Application Instructions Non-exempt positions must be posted for a minimum of five (5) days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice. Required application documents: resume/CV, transcripts, and cover letter . Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. *Sponsorship funding is not available for this position ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer University Overview (as needed) East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1385": {
      "title": "Patient Care Representative - Center for Outpatient Rehab",
      "description": "Category: Medical Practice JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States Description Job Summary The Patient Care Representative serves as the primary point of contact for patients within the Outpatient Rehabilitation Clinic, supporting efficient and patient-centered clinical operations. This position is responsible for appointment scheduling, patient registration, electronic medical record maintenance, billing and collections support, and front-desk financial transactions while ensuring compliance with HIPAA and institutional policies. Working closely with clinical providers, students, and the Office Coordinator, the Patient Care Representative contributes to smooth patient flow, accurate documentation, and high-quality service delivery in a fast-paced healthcare environment serving a diverse patient population. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of electronic health and electronic practice management. Knowledge of Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial insurance. Ability to use electronic records and practice management systems. Ability to process office supply orders. Ability to be flexible in adjusting and implementing changes in protocol, procedures, and workflow. Ability to use business English in written and verbal communication. Ability to perform data entry accurately. Ability to function as a team player in a patient-centered health care setting. Ability to learn and effectively utilize electronic health records and practice management software. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions. Ability to use proper telephone etiquette. Ability to follow proper policies, procedures, and instructions in accomplishing tasks. Ability to work with a diverse population, along with the ability to treat all patients and co-workers with dignity and respect. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Two years of medical office experience or at least one year of post-high school course-level work with one year of medical office experience Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Medical Clinical Associate 1 MR - 3 For information on benefits, please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Non exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter, Resume, and three (3) references available upon request University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students and highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer Disclaimer Statement: Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1390": {
      "title": "Coordinator (COM - Rural Programs)",
      "description": "Category: Medical Practice JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary This position resides in Quillen College of Medicine’s Rural and Community Programs division. A division dedicated to educating future physicians, especially those with an interest in primary care, to practice in underserved/rural communities. This role will coordinate the Underserved Medicine Clerkship utilized by Generalist Track students during the clinical phase of their education. This position will require an individual with an interest in community engagement, a passion for working with students, and a desire to make an impact. This position directly reports to the Administrator of Rural and Community Programs and is advised by the Associate Dean for Rural and Community Programs for programmatic needs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of the medical education system is preferred. Knowledge of computers, with strong skills in word processing, Ability to engage communities, build community partnerships, and develop preceptor relationships for student involvement. Ability to manage time appropriately to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Ability to be organized and handle multiple responsibilities simultaneously. Ability to deal professionally and responsibly with privileged information. Ability to travel on a limited basis with some overnight stays. Competent in the Microsoft Office suite including MS Teams. Strong communication skills (both verbal and written). Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or higher. Two (2) years of experience in a role requiring autonomy. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of experience in a healthcare-related field or field of medical education Compensation and Benefits Job Family – Medical Academic Professional 1E Salary – MR 6 ($47,002.36) For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions Exempt positions are required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. This is subject to change without notice to the applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter and Resume *This is not a remote position University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For , recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
