    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1386": {
      "title": "Temporary Part-Time Research Technician",
      "description": "Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary: The Department of Biomedical Sciences in the College of Medicine at East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Research Technician for a Temporary Hourly Part-Time position. The anticipated start date for this position is in January of 2027. In this vital role, you will join Dr. Qian Xie’s research laboratory, contributing to innovative biological research experiments and supporting the lab’s ongoing projects. This position involves performing a variety of technical duties related to standardized tests and experiments. Key Responsibilities: Perform technical duties of a physical or biological nature to support research activities Assist with data collection, interpretation, evaluation, and documentation for lab projects Operate and set up laboratory or research equipment for experiments Collect, tabulate, and calculate data using various electronic devices, Maintain computer databases of research and protocol records, Order, replace, and maintain laboratory supplies, Conduct minor repairs on research equipment as needed, Perform general laboratory maintenance and cleanup, Train and supervise new research personnel, Occasional evening, weekend, and holiday work may be required, Carry out additional duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of basic laboratory methodology. Knowledge of business English and arithmetic. Ability to perform basic informational research projects. Ability to gather, compile, and analyze data. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues and the public. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Excel. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience working with rodent models. Previous laboratory experience. Important Notes: This position is based on-site and is not eligible for remote work. Please note that sponsorship is not available for this position. Compensation: Salary Range: $­­20.00 to $23.00 per hour - based on experience Application Requirements & Conditions: The following documents are required to apply. Include with your application: Cover Letter , Resume , and Three (3) References that include their phone number and e-mail address. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Employment is contingent upon approved work authorization. Employment is contingent upon sufficient grant funding. Non-Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer. University Overview: East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1388": {
      "title": "Clinical Education Partner",
      "description": "Category: Medical Practice JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: United States The Department of Internal Medicine seeks applicants for the role of Clinical Education Partner . This individual will establish and maintain regular communication with community physicians, clinical site leadership, and educational partners to ensure each location has the resources, support, and information necessary to successfully fulfill the educational mission of both the Department and the College of Medicine. This position will conduct routine site visits to affiliated clinical locations, serving as the department's primary point of contact for educational matters. In addition to serving as the Department's educational liaison, this position will dedicate roughly half of their professional time to coordinating and supporting the Department's Cardiology Fellowship Program and providing administrative support to other fellowship programs as they continue to expand. Key Responsibilities Include: Serves as the primary liaison to affiliated clinical education sites, building and maintaining relationships with community physicians, preceptors, and site leadership Conducts site visits and outreach to assess educational needs, provide resources, and address operational concerns affecting clinical education. Coordinates onboarding and orientation of community faculty, including appointments, required documentation, and access to educational platforms and departmental resources. Supports UME and GME initiatives across affiliated sites, including distribution of educational materials, policy updates, and accreditation documentation such as Program Letters of Agreement (PLAs). Collaborates with clerkship directors, residency and fellowship leadership, and departmental administration to improve learner experiences, strengthen site engagement, and resolve educational and operational challenges. Coordinates fellowship program administration, including schedules, records, correspondence, meetings, reports, and communication among program leadership, faculty, and trainees. Manages trainee onboarding, offboarding, appointments, credentialing, licensing, required training, graduation, and transition activities; serves as a primary resource for fellows regarding program policies and institutional requirements. Coordinates fellowship recruitment, including ERAS administration, applicant communications, interview scheduling, selection, and match processes in accordance with institutional, ACGME, and NRMP requirements. Supports fellowship curriculum implementation, conferences, evaluations, trainee assessments, milestone reporting, program evaluations, and competency committee documentation. Coordinates program finances and logistics, including travel, reimbursements, purchasing, and conference registration. Maintains accreditation records, trainee files, evaluations, and program data; supports the Program Director with ACGME accreditation preparation, Accreditation Data System (ADS) updates, annual reporting, and ongoing compliance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of UME, GME, fellowship operations, and medical education principles. Knowledge of ACGME accreditation standards, institutional policies, and compliance requirements. Knowledge of clinical education site operations, community faculty engagement, and academic-clinical partnerships. Knowledge of trainee recruitment, onboarding, evaluation, assessment, and program administration. Skill in managing educational technology platforms, program data, accreditation documentation, and reporting. Skill in building effective relationships and communicating professionally with faculty, trainees, clinical sites, and institutional partners. Skill in coordinating multiple projects, prioritizing competing demands, and meeting deadlines independently. Skill in problem-solving, resolving operational issues, and supporting continuous program improvement. Ability to interpret and apply accreditation standards, institutional policies, and program requirements while maintaining confidentiality and sound judgment. Ability to travel regularly between clinical sites and academic offices while supporting learner success, faculty engagement, and program quality. Required Qualifications: Associate's Degree Three (3) years of relevant experience ( i.e. healthcare, academics, education, program management, community programs, etc.) -OR- an equivalent combination of education and experience Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in healthcare administration, education, public health, or related field Five (5) years of relevant experience (i.e. healthcare, academics, education, program management, community programs, etc.) Experience supporting a medical education program, including fellowship, residency, clerkship, or other health profession education programs -OR- an equivalent combination of education and experience Compensation and Benefits: Job Family- Medical Academic Professional 1 Salary- MR6- ($47,002.36) For more information regarding benefits, please visit ( Employee Benefits ) Application Instructions: Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to the applicants. This position is contingent on a satisfactory background check. Please attach the following documents: Cover Letter and Resume Important Notes: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position This position requires on-site work and the ability to travel between multiple clinical sites each week University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution’s mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. ETSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer Disclaimer Statement: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employee must be able to perform the essential functions of the position satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1389": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor, Community & Behavioral Health",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary The Clinical Instructor serves the Department of Community and Behavioral Health by providing high-quality instruction, student mentorship, and community-engaged learning experiences across undergraduate, master's, and doctoral public health programs. The position is a nine-month, teaching-focused faculty appointment that supports undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral education while providing operational leadership for Project EARTH. Responsibilities include classroom and online instruction, dissertation committee service, community engagement activities, student mentoring, experiential learning initiatives, and support for student organizations and academic outreach efforts. The Clinical Instructor will support recruitment and retention efforts, and enhance the department's capacity to meet increasing instructional and doctoral education demands. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to teach effectively in undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral-level public health programs. Knowledge of public health principles, program planning, evaluation, and community health practice. Ability to develop and facilitate experiential and service-learning opportunities. Ability to teach in face-to-face, hybrid, and online environments. Ability to mentor undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students. Working knowledge of low-resource and community-based health settings. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to collaborate with faculty, students, community partners, and external stakeholders. Ability to support student organizations, recruitment activities, and community engagement initiatives. Ability to serve on doctoral dissertation committees and mentor graduate students. Required Qualifications Doctor of Public Health (DrPH) or closely related terminal degree from an accredited institution. Demonstrated history of experiential learning and community-engaged education. Working knowledge of low-resource health settings. Experience supporting extracurricular student activities and student engagement initiatives. Ability to teach across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs. Eligibility for graduate faculty status. Preferred Qualifications Experience in public health higher education. Experience with online instruction and course delivery. Experience serving on graduate thesis or dissertation committees. Experience developing community partnerships and service-learning opportunities. Experience with global health, community health, or public health practice programs. Physical Demands (as needed) Regular use of computers and instructional technology. Occasional travel to schools, community sites, and Project EARTH locations. Ability to conduct field-based educational and community engagement activities. Ability to carry 50 lbs. Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1392": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Biomedical Health Sciences)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary East Tennessee State University – Department of Biomedical Health Sciences – Assistant Professor – Anatomy and Physiology – position #206260. The Department of Biomedical Health Sciences, in the College of Public Health, at East Tennessee State University, seeks applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor level opening beginning August 2027. Teaching responsibilities will include undergraduate Anatomy and Physiology I and II and Human Genetics. The candidate will have the opportunity to teach or develop other courses depending on the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs. The primary focus of this position is that of teaching, but the successful candidate is expected to conduct scholarly activity related to their expertise and which are in line with the mission of the Department and College. The initial teaching load for the position is expected to be 2 courses (lectures + labs) per semester. Participation on committees at the Department, College, and University levels is also required. A PhD in a relevant field is required. The preferred applicant will have experience in teaching undergraduate health sciences courses, with evidence of effectiveness in teaching undergraduate anatomy/physiology. Two years of undergraduate teaching with independent teaching experience preferred. GA teaching experience will also be considered. Applicants with experience in teaching human genetics will receive extra consideration. Applicants with postdoctoral experience in a relevant field or with extensive teaching experience or pedagogical research will receive extra consideration. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience in teaching undergraduate health sciences courses Evidence of effectiveness in teaching undergraduate anatomy and physiology Required Qualifications Earned PhD in a relevant field Preferred Qualifications Two years of undergraduate teaching with independent teaching experience preferred Experience in teaching human genetics Postdoctoral experience in a relevant field Extensive teaching experience or pedagogical research Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 5 Salary is commensurate on experience For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter, CV and Transcripts. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1393": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Lab Coordinator) - Biomedical Health Sciences",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary College of Public Health – Department of Biomedical Health Sciences- Lecturer/ Laboratory Coordinator Level 7- 251610. The Lecturer/Lab Coordinator will be responsible for teaching Introduction to Microbiology. Other essential functions include being responsible for coordinating the laboratories for Introduction to Microbiology, General Microbiology, Bacterial Physiology, Pathogenic Microbiology, and Biochemistry. Duties include lab setup, lab cleanup, preparation of media, microorganisms, and solutions, as well as maintenance and ordering of equipment/chemicals/supplies and other materials as needed. Providing support to the other teaching needs of the department will be required. In addition, training and supervision of undergraduate/graduate students and staff is required. This position also serves as support to faculty performing research in the Department of Biomedical Health Sciences. Other duties may be assigned as deemed necessary. Qualifications: M.S. in Microbiology or Biological Sciences, with PhD preferred. Undergraduate teaching experience preferred. GA teaching experience will be considered. The successful applicant will be proficient with a variety of laboratory research equipment and procedures. High proficiency in aseptic technique as well as proficiency with computers, esp. word processors and spreadsheet programs, is required. Good organization skills and the ability to work well with others and are required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with a variety of laboratory research equipment and procedures High proficiency in aseptic technique Proficiency with computers, esp. word processors and spreadsheet programs Good organization skills and the ability to work well with others Required Qualifications M.S. in Microbiology or Biological Sciences, with PhD preferred. Preferred Qualifications Undergraduate teaching experience Experience with a variety of laboratory research equipment and procedures High proficiency in aseptic technique Proficiency with computers, esp. word processors and spreadsheet programs Good organization skills and the ability to work well with others Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Academic Faculty 3 Salary is commensurate on experience For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. Documents needed to apply: Cover Letter, CV and Transcripts ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
