    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1402": {
      "title": "Internal/Family Medicine Faculty",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Posting Summary The ETSU Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice, invites applications for a 12-month faculty position in Inpatient Internal/Family Medicine. This faculty role offers the opportunity to contribute to pharmacy education, clinical practice, and service while working in a collaborative healthcare environment. The position may be based at either Johnson City Medical Center (JCMC) or Holston Valley Medical Center (HVMC). Interested candidates should apply online at https://jobs.etsu.edu . Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to: Provide evidence-informed, patient-centered inpatient pharmacy care as part of an interprofessional team. Communicate effectively with patients, caregivers, pharmacists, physicians, learners, and other health professionals. Teach and mentor student pharmacists and pharmacy residents in clinical and classroom settings. Develop and contribute to scholarly work and presentations relevant to pharmacy practice and education. Work collaboratively across ETSU and Ballad Health while supporting the College’s rural and underserved health mission. Required Qualifications Applicants must have: A PharmD or other terminal pharmacy degree. Completion of a PGY2 residency (internal medicine or pharmacotherapy preferred) by summer 2027. Eligibility for pharmacist licensure in Tennessee. Demonstrated excellence in clinical practice and a strong interest in teaching and scholarship in an academic environment. Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to candidates with experience in inpatient internal medicine or family medicine, Certification from the Board of Pharmacy Specialties (BPS), experience precepting learners, and a record of scholarly activity. Compensation and Benefits Salary: Competitive with AACP faculty salaries and commensurate with qualifications and experience. For information on benefits, please visit: https://www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. About Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy East Tennessee State University (ETSU) Bill Gatton College of Pharmacy offers nationally-recognized pharmacy training in Johnson City, Tennessee. The Class of 2025's first-attempt pass rates on the North American Pharmacist Licensure Examination (NAPLEX) and Multistate Pharmacy Jurisprudence Examination (MPJE) placed the College among the top five accredited pharmacy schools in the nation and No. 1 in Tennessee. These accomplishments are the result of Gatton’s student-centered culture. Exceptional faculty prepare students through a curriculum designed for practice as collaborative members of the health care team, and students translate that preparation into national leadership and service. The College is part of ETSU Health, Tennessee’s largest public academic health sciences center. At its core, Gatton’s mission is to improve health care in rural and underserved communities. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1410": {
      "title": "Supervisor, Maintenance of Grounds",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Under general direction, supervises and performs a variety of grounds maintenance, landscaping, road and sidewalk repairs, and campus maintenance activities to ensure the campus grounds, streets, and walkways are safe, clean, functional, and well-maintained. Responsibilities include mowing, trimming, pruning, planting, brush management, tree and shrub care, snow removal, parking lot maintenance, pavement marking, traffic sign installation, equipment operation, mechanical repairs, and event support. Receives and reviews work orders, plans and assigns daily tasks, demonstrates proper work methods, monitors work in progress and upon completion, and trains new employees to ensure work is performed safely, efficiently, and in accordance with established standards. Performs other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of the methods, materials, tools, equipment, and practices used in grounds maintenance. Knowledge of basic landscaping techniques and procedures. Ability to plan work schedules, prioritize tasks, and assign duties effectively. Ability to direct, monitor, and inspect the work of others to ensure quality and completion. Ability to demonstrate proper work methods and provide guidance to employees as needed. Ability to maintain adequate inventories of supplies, materials, tools, and equipment. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with coworkers, supervisors, and other campus personnel. Required Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and a minimum of six months of relevant experience in grounds maintenance, landscaping, equipment operation, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Possession of a valid Tennessee driver's license. May require specialized training or certifications related to equipment operation, grounds maintenance, or other assigned duties Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services Buildings and Grounds Assistant 3 Starting Salary: MR4 Salary Schedules For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Non-Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of five (5) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1411": {
      "title": "Utility Worker - Driver",
      "description": "Category: Facilities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Job Summary Under general supervision, this position is responsible for maintaining athletic and recreational grounds across campus. Duties include mowing, trimming, weeding, bed maintenance, litter pickup, field painting, and preparing fields for games and events. Work areas include the soccer and softball fields, golf facility, intramural fields, walking track, and ropes course. The role involves operating light motor vehicles and turf equipment such as mowers, weed eaters, tractors, and blowers. Candidates should demonstrate basic turf care knowledge, effective time management, and the ability to work independently in all weather conditions. This is considered an essential personnel position during inclement weather. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to manage time, to ensure all tasks are completed in a given time. Ability to demonstrate good communication skills. Ability to operate the following equipment: Reel Mowers, Scag Mower, Weed eater, push Mower, hand Tools, Hand Sprayer, Fertilizer Spreader, Tractor, Blower, and Utility Vehicles. Specialized Skills in mowing direction, patterns, and utilization of Turf Mowers. Ability to produce a high-quality result in all aspects of Turf maintenance duties. Ability to work in adverse conditions all seasons of the year. Knowledge and Ability to perform many different specialized tasks pertaining to horticulture, Athletic Fields, and Turf Maintenance. Required Qualifications High school/GED Possess and maintain a valid Driver License. Preferred Qualifications Experience in turf maintenance preferred. Physical Demands (as needed) Perform strenuous physical work on a daily basis Work outdoors in adverse weather conditions year-round Lift, carry, and maneuver equipment and materials as needed Perform repetitive motions such as bending, lifting, kneeling, and climbing Stand and walk for extended periods of time Compensation & Benefits Job Family – Facilities Services Buildings and Grounds Assistant 2 Starting Salary: MR3 Salary Schedules For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    },
    "https://fa-evyu-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1417": {
      "title": "Software Engineer",
      "description": "Category: Information Technology JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States **This is an on-site position at ETSU and is not eligible for remote work.** Job Summary Reporting to the Assistant Chief Information Officer for Enterprise Software and Services, the Software Engineer develops, administers, integrates, and enhances enterprise applications supporting Human Resources, Finance, Payroll, Financial Aid, and Student Services. Working collaboratively with ITS staff and functional stakeholders, the position translates business and technical requirements into reliable, secure, and efficient solutions across Ellucian Student, Oracle Fusion Cloud HCM/ERP, and related systems. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of cloud computing service models, including Software as a Service (SaaS), Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), and Platform as a Service (PaaS). Knowledge of React and C# within the .NET framework. Knowledge of and skill in using GraphQL and SQL to access, query, and manage data along with scripting of basic complexity. Proficiency with version control systems, preferably GIT. Demonstrated experience developing web-based applications. Skill in using API clients and testing tools, such as Postman or Bruno, to test, troubleshoot, and validate integrations. Ability to independently investigate, analyze, and resolve technical issues with initiative and sound judgment. Ability to work independently and collaborate effectively within a team. Ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing operational needs. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computing, Engineering, or related field and one (1) year of relevant work experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Oracle Integration Cloud. Experience with configuration of Oracle Fusion Cloud environments (specifically HCM and ERP). Experience with configuration of Oracle Enterprise Performance Management (EPM, formerly Hyperion). Experience with Ellucian Banner products. Experience with UNIX/Linux based operating systems. Demonstrated experience with shell scripting of basic complexity. Compensation & Benefits Job Family – IT Administrator/Analyst 1 Market Range: 8 ( Salary Schedules ) For information on benefits please visit www.etsu.edu/human-resources/benefits/ . Application Instructions Exempt positions are only required to be posted for a minimum of fourteen (14) calendar days. The closing date for this posting is subject to change without notice to applicants. Employment contingent on a satisfactory background check. ETSU is an equal opportunity employer. University Overview East Tennessee State University (ETSU) is an institution with over 14,000 diverse students highly ranked graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in the Southern Appalachian Mountains of Northeast Tennessee, ETSU serves as a hub for community, discovery, and service. Aligned with the institution's mission, we value efforts to engage in teaching, scholarship, creative activities, and service that involve community partners and address significant societal needs in our region and beyond. Recognized in 2024 as a Great College to Work For, recent strategic initiatives prioritize the institution’s focus on community engagement. Disclaimer: The Job Summary is intended to describe the general nature and level of work individuals perform in this classification. It is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require different tasks to be performed as assigned to reflect changes in the position. Employees must be able to perform the position's essential functions satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. "
    }
